{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2of5v6wh7vyiww56n7mfjg7dwgygsypsvyo3hjr5wg7virybadfa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## 1. `zstd_legacy.h` — gating and dispatch\n\nFile: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust/c_src/src/legacy/zstd_legacy.h` (453 lines)\n\n### Default fallback (lines 25-28)\nIf `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT` is undefined or `0`, it is redefined to `8` (i.e. no legacy at all).\n\n### Include gating (lines 30-50) — all `<=` comparisons\n\n| guard | include |\n|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT <= 1` | `zstd_v01.h` |\n| `<= 2` | `zstd_v02.h` |\n| `<= 3` | `zstd_v03.h` |\n| `<= 4` | `zstd_v04.h` |\n| `<= 5` | `zstd_v05.h` |\n| `<= 6` | `zstd_v06.h` |\n| `<= 7` | `zstd_v07.h` |\n\n### With the build's `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5` (`c_src/CMakeLists.txt:22`)\n\nOnly `zstd_v05.h`, `zstd_v06.h`, `zstd_v07.h` are included. The dispatch code therefore references **only v05, v06, v07** symbols. v01–v04 are compiled *out* of every dispatch function.\n\nActual dispatch function names in this header (note: not exactly the names in the request):\n\n| requested name | actual name in C | line |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_isLegacy` | `ZSTD_isLegacy` | 56 |\n| `ZSTD_getDecompressedSizeLegacy` | **`ZSTD_getDecompressedSize_legacy`** | 89 |\n| `ZSTD_decompressLegacy` | `ZSTD_decompressLegacy` | 121 |\n| `ZSTD_getFrameSizeLegacy` | **`ZSTD_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy`** (+ wrapper `ZSTD_findFrameCompressedSizeLegacy`) | 195, 269 |\n| `ZSTD_freeLegacyStreamContext` | `ZSTD_freeLegacyStreamContext` | 275 |\n| `ZSTD_initLegacyStream` | `ZSTD_initLegacyStream` | 301 |\n| `ZSTD_decompressLegacyStream` | `ZSTD_decompressLegacyStream` | 366 |\n\nAll are `MEM_STATIC` (header-inline, **not** exported symbols — they do not appear in `SYMBOLS.md`). Sole consumers: `c_src/src/decompress/zstd_decompress.c` (lines 334, 393, 572-573, 740-741, 1090-1097, 2133, 2144, 2152, 2156) and the include in `c_src/src/decompress/zstd_ddict.c:28`.\n\nWhich versions survive at `=5`:\n\n| function | v01 | v02 | v03 | v04 | v05 | v06 | v07 | behavior for excluded versions |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_isLegacy` | no | no | no | no | **yes → 5** | **yes → 6** | **yes → 7** | falls to `default : return 0` |\n| `ZSTD_getDecompressedSize_legacy` | no | no | no | no | **yes** | **yes** | **yes** | early `if (version < 5) return 0;` |\n| `ZSTD_decompressLegacy` | no | no | no | no | **yes** | **yes** | **yes** | `default : return ERROR(prefix_unknown)` |\n| `ZSTD_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy` | no | no | no | no | **yes** | **yes** | **yes** | `default:` → `ERROR(prefix_unknown)` + `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_ERROR` |\n| `ZSTD_freeLegacyStreamContext` | no | no | no | no | **yes** | **yes** | **yes** | `default: case 1: case 2: case 3:` → `ERROR(version_unsupported)`; **case 4 is compiled out at =5, so version 4 also falls through to `ERROR(version_unsupported)`** |\n| `ZSTD_initLegacyStream` | no | no | no | no | **yes** | **yes** | **yes** | `default: case 1..3:` → `return 0` (silently no-op); version 4 also lands here at =5 |\n| `ZSTD_decompressLegacyStream` | no | no | no | no | **yes** | **yes** | **yes** | `default: case 1..3:` → `ERROR(version_unsupported)`; version 4 too at =5 |\n\n### How `ZSTD_isLegacy` derives the version (lines 56-86)\n`magicNumberLE = MEM_readLE32(src)` (returns 0 if `srcSize < 4`), then a `switch` returning the version number directly. Note the asymmetry — v01 matches the **LE-spelled** constant because v0.1 frames wrote the magic big-endian (`zstd_v01.c:1267` `ZSTD_magicNumber = 0xFD2FB51E` read via `ZSTD_readBE32`):\n\n| case label | value | returns |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTDv01_magicNumberLE` | `0x1EB52FFD` (`ZSTDv01_magicNumber` = `0xFD2FB51E` BE) | 1 |\n| `ZSTDv02_magicNumber` | `0xFD2FB522` | 2 |\n| `ZSTDv03_magicNumber` | `0xFD2FB523` | 3 |\n| `ZSTDv04_magicNumber` | `0xFD2FB524` | 4 |\n| `ZSTDv05_MAGICNUMBER` | `0xFD2FB525` | 5 |\n| `ZSTDv06_MAGICNUMBER` | `0xFD2FB526` | 6 |\n| `ZSTDv07_MAGICNUMBER` | `0xFD2FB527` | 7 |\n\n### IMPORTANT nuance: the `.c` files ARE still fully compiled\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` uses `file(GLOB ... \"src/legacy/*.c\")`, and **none** of `zstd_v01.c` … `zstd_v07.c` has an `#if (ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT <= N)` guard around its body. Verified: `grep ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT` matches only in `zstd_v02.c:2604` and `zstd_v03.c:2242`, and those are a vestigial `#ifndef ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT / # define ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT 1` block inherited from the original v0.2/v0.3 amalgamated sources — not a body guard. `zstd_v01.c`, `zstd_v04.c`, `zstd_v05.c`, `zstd_v06.c`, `zstd_v07.c` contain no occurrence at all.\n\nConsequence: **all seven versions' object code and exported symbols exist in `libzstd.so` even at `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5`; they are simply unreachable through the dispatch.** Confirmed by `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust/SYMBOLS.md`, which lists `ZSTDv01_decompress`, `ZSTDv02_decompress`, `ZSTDv03_decompress`, `ZSTDv04_decompress` (lines 563, 572, 580, 588) plus all `ZBUFFv04_*` (lines 214-222). `SYMBOLS.md:24` reports `ZSTDv0*` = 91 C / 91 Rust, and `ZBUFF*` = 58 (37 of which are `ZBUFFv0[4-7]_*`).\n\n### Dict handling in `ZSTD_decompressLegacy`\n\nSignature (lines 121-124): `(void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t compressedSize, const void* dict, size_t dictSize)` — yes, it takes a dict.\n\n| version | dict used? |\n|---|---|\n| 1, 2, 3, 4 | **ignored silently** — calls `ZSTDv0N_decompress(dst, dstCapacity, src, compressedSize)` with no dict param; no error raised (also `(void)dict; (void)dictSize;` at line 141) |\n| 5 | **used** — `ZSTDv05_decompress_usingDict(zd, ..., dict, dictSize)` |\n| 6 | **used** — `ZSTDv06_decompress_usingDict(...)` |\n| 7 | **used** — `ZSTDv07_decompress_usingDict(...)` |\n\nNULL-avoidance: `dst`, `src`, `dict` are each repointed at a stack `char x` when NULL (asserting the corresponding size is 0). `ZSTD_initLegacyStream` does the same for `dict`; `ZSTD_decompressLegacyStream` does it for `output->dst`/`input->src` using a `static char x`.\n\nDict in streaming (`ZSTD_initLegacyStream`): v1-3 (and v4 at `=5`) `(void)dict; (void)dictSize; return 0;` — no error, dict dropped. v4 (when compiled) uses `ZBUFFv04_decompressInit` + `ZBUFFv04_decompressWithDictionary`. v5/6/7 use `ZBUFFv0N_decompressInitDictionary`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Per-version exported public symbols\n\nLegend: **H** = declared in `zstd_v0N.h`; **S** = present in `SYMBOLS.md`. `H-only` = declared in header but never defined in the `.c`, therefore **not** an exported symbol. `S-only` = exported but declared only in the `*_STATIC_LINKING_ONLY` block embedded in the `.c`, not in the public `.h`.\n\n### v01 — `zstd_v01.h` (9 H / 9 S, exact match)\n- one-shot: `ZSTDv01_decompress`, `ZSTDv01_decompressDCtx`\n- frame size info: `ZSTDv01_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy`\n- ctx mgmt: `ZSTDv01_createDCtx`, `ZSTDv01_freeDCtx`\n- streaming (direct): `ZSTDv01_resetDCtx`, `ZSTDv01_nextSrcSizeToDecompress`, `ZSTDv01_decompressContinue`\n- ZBUFF: **none**\n- dict entry points: **none**\n- errors/magic: `ZSTDv01_isError`; macros `ZSTDv01_magicNumber` (`0xFD2FB51E`), `ZSTDv01_magicNumberLE` (`0x1EB52FFD`)\n- opaque type: `ZSTDv01_Dctx` / `struct ZSTDv01_Dctx_s`\n\n### v02 — `zstd_v02.h` (9 H / **8 S**)\n- one-shot: `ZSTDv02_decompress`; `ZSTDv02_decompressDCtx` → **H-only, NOT exported** (declared `zstd_v02.h:64`, no definition in `zstd_v02.c`)\n- frame size info: `ZSTDv02_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy`\n- ctx mgmt: `ZSTDv02_createDCtx`, `ZSTDv02_freeDCtx`\n- streaming: `ZSTDv02_resetDCtx`, `ZSTDv02_nextSrcSizeToDecompress`, `ZSTDv02_decompressContinue`\n- ZBUFF / dict: **none**\n- errors/magic: `ZSTDv02_isError`; `ZSTDv02_magicNumber` = `0xFD2FB522`\n- type: `ZSTDv02_Dctx`\n\n### v03 — `zstd_v03.h` (9 H / **8 S**)\n- one-shot: `ZSTDv03_decompress`; `ZSTDv03_decompressDCtx` → **H-only, NOT exported** (`zstd_v03.h:64`)\n- frame size info: `ZSTDv03_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy`\n- ctx mgmt: `ZSTDv03_createDCtx`, `ZSTDv03_freeDCtx`\n- streaming: `ZSTDv03_resetDCtx`, `ZSTDv03_nextSrcSizeToDecompress`, `ZSTDv03_decompressContinue`\n- ZBUFF / dict: **none**\n- errors/magic: `ZSTDv03_isError`; `ZSTDv03_magicNumber` = `0xFD2FB523`\n- type: `ZSTDv03_Dctx`\n\n### v04 — `zstd_v04.h` (`ZSTDv04_*`: 9 H / **8 S**; `ZBUFFv04_*`: 9 H / 9 S)\n- one-shot: `ZSTDv04_decompress`, `ZSTDv04_decompressDCtx`\n- frame size info: `ZSTDv04_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy`\n- ctx mgmt: `ZSTDv04_createDCtx`, `ZSTDv04_freeDCtx`\n- streaming (direct): `ZSTDv04_resetDCtx`, `ZSTDv04_nextSrcSizeToDecompress`, `ZSTDv04_decompressContinue`\n- ZBUFF streaming: `ZBUFFv04_createDCtx`, `ZBUFFv04_freeDCtx`, `ZBUFFv04_decompressInit`, `ZBUFFv04_decompressWithDictionary`, `ZBUFFv04_decompressContinue`, `ZBUFFv04_isError`, `ZBUFFv04_getErrorName`, `ZBUFFv04_recommendedDInSize`, `ZBUFFv04_recommendedDOutSize`\n- dict entry points: **only** `ZBUFFv04_decompressWithDictionary` (streaming). The one-shot path has no public dict API — the internal `static size_t ZSTD_decompress_usingDict(...)` (`zstd_v04.c:3006`) is called with `NULL, 0` from `ZSTDv04_decompressDCtx` (`zstd_v04.c:3552`)\n- errors/magic: `ZSTDv04_isError` → **H-only, NOT exported** (declared `zstd_v04.h:54`, never defined; `grep` finds no definition anywhere). `ZSTDv04_magicNumber` = `0xFD2FB524`\n- types: `ZSTDv04_Dctx`, `ZBUFFv04_DCtx`\n\n### v05 — `zstd_v05.h` (`ZSTDv05_*`: 17 S; `ZBUFFv05_*`: 9 H / 9 S)\n- one-shot: `ZSTDv05_decompress`, `ZSTDv05_decompressDCtx`\n- frame size info / params: `ZSTDv05_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy`, `ZSTDv05_getFrameParams` (fills `ZSTDv05_parameters`, whose `.srcSize` is what `ZSTD_getDecompressedSize_legacy` returns)\n- ctx mgmt: `ZSTDv05_createDCtx`, `ZSTDv05_freeDCtx`, `ZSTDv05_copyDCtx`\n- streaming (direct): `ZSTDv05_nextSrcSizeToDecompress`, `ZSTDv05_decompressContinue`, `ZSTDv05_decompressBegin_usingDict`; **S-only** (from the static-linking block in `zstd_v0