equences` | `ZSTD_c_nbWorkers != 0` on the cctx | `ZSTD_error_parameter_unsupported` |\n| `ZSTD_generateSequences` | `ZSTD_customMalloc(ZSTD_compressBound(srcSize))` returns NULL | `ZSTD_error_memory_allocation` |\n| `ZSTD_generateSequences` | `srcSize >= ZSTD_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` so `ZSTD_compressBound()` errors → huge malloc | `ZSTD_error_memory_allocation` (malloc of an error-code-sized buffer fails) |\n| `ZSTD_generateSequences` | `outSeqsSize` too small to hold all sequences + delimiters (`< ZSTD_sequenceBound(srcSize)`) | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_generateSequences` | any error from the underlying `ZSTD_compress2` | that error, forwarded |\n| `ZSTD_mergeBlockDelimiters` | any input (incl. `seqsSize == 0`) | never errors; returns count of non-delimiter sequences (`0` if all were delimiters) |\n| `ZSTD_validateSequence` (only when `ZSTD_c_validateSequences==1`) | `offBase > OFFSET_TO_OFFBASE(offsetBound)` where `offsetBound = posInSrc > (1<<windowLog) ? (1<<windowLog) : posInSrc + dictSize` | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` |\n| `ZSTD_validateSequence` | `matchLength < ((minMatch==3 \\|\\| extSeqProd) ? 3 : 4)` | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` |\n| `ZSTD_transferSequences_wBlockDelim` (`ZSTD_c_blockDelimiters == ZSTD_sf_explicitBlockDelimiters`) | `idx - seqPos->idx >= cctx->seqStore.maxNbSeq` (too many seqs for the allocated seqStore) | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` |\n| `ZSTD_transferSequences_wBlockDelim` | loop consumed all of `inSeqs` without hitting a `(offset==0 && matchLength==0)` delimiter | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` (\"Block delimiter not found\") |\n| `ZSTD_transferSequences_wBlockDelim` | after consuming the block, `ip != iend` (sum of lit+match lengths ≠ blockSize) | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` |\n| `ZSTD_transferSequences_noDelim` (`ZSTD_sf_noBlockDelimiters`) | `idx - seqPos->idx >= cctx->seqStore.maxNbSeq` | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` |\n| `blockSize_explicitDelimiter` (via `ZSTD_compressSequences`) | a sequence has `offset == 0` but `matchLength != 0` | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` (\"both matchlength and offset must be == 0\") |\n| `blockSize_explicitDelimiter` | reached end of `inSeqs` with no delimiter | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` |\n| `determine_blockSize` (explicit delimiters) | `explicitBlockSize > cctx->blockSizeMax` | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` (\"too large a block\") |\n| `determine_blockSize` (explicit delimiters) | `explicitBlockSize > remaining` (sequences describe more bytes than `srcSize`) | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` (\"frame longer than source\") |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequences_internal` | `srcSize == 0` && `dstCapacity < 4` | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequences_internal` | `blockSize < 7` (too small) && `dstCapacity < blockSize + 3` | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` (from `ZSTD_noCompressBlock`) |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequences_internal` | `dstCapacity < ZSTD_blockHeaderSize` (3) before a compressed block | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequences_internal` | RLE path chosen and `dstCapacity < 4` | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` (from `ZSTD_rleCompressBlock`) |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequences` | `ZSTD_CCtx_init_compressStream2` fails (bad dict, alloc failure, ext-seq-prod + nbWorkers) | that error, forwarded |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequences` | `dstCapacity < 18` (`ZSTD_writeFrameHeader`) | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequences` | `fParams.checksumFlag` && remaining `dstCapacity < 4` | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals` | `litCapacity < litSize` | `ZSTD_error_workSpace_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals` | `appliedParams.blockDelimiters == ZSTD_sf_noBlockDelimiters` | `ZSTD_error_frameParameter_unsupported` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals` | `appliedParams.validateSequences != 0` (`ZSTD_c_validateSequences==1`) | `ZSTD_error_parameter_unsupported` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals` | `appliedParams.fParams.checksumFlag != 0` (`ZSTD_c_checksumFlag==1`) | `ZSTD_error_frameParameter_unsupported` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals` | `dstCapacity < 18` (frame header) | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals_internal` | `nbSequences == 0` | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` (\"Requires at least 1 end-of-block\") |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals_internal` | `nbSequences==1 && inSeqs[0].litLength==0` (empty frame) && `dstCapacity < 3` | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals_internal` | `block.litSize > litSize` (sequences need more literals than supplied) | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals_internal` | `dstCapacity < ZSTD_blockHeaderSize` (3) before a block | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals_internal` | entropy coding produced `compressedSeqsSize == 0`, or `> cctx->blockSizeMax` (forced to 0) — i.e. block is incompressible and the source is unavailable | `ZSTD_error_cannotProduce_uncompressedBlock` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals_internal` | after all blocks, `litSize != 0` (literals left over) | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals_internal` | after all blocks, `remaining != 0` (sequences don't sum to `decompressedSize`) | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` |\n| `ZSTD_get1BlockSummary` (via `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals`) | scanned all `nbSeqs` without finding a `matchLength == 0` end-of-block marker | `bs.nbSequences = ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` (forwarded as an error) |\n| `ZSTD_convertBlockSequences` | `nbSequences >= cctx->seqStore.maxNbSeq` | `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` (\"Try adjusting ZSTD_c_minMatch\") |\n| `ZSTD_getFrameProgression` | any | never errors (returns a struct); MT path delegates to `ZSTDMT_getFrameProgression` |\n| `ZSTD_toFlushNow` | single-threaded context | `0` (over-simplification, not an error) |\n| `ZSTD_registerSequenceProducer` / `ZSTD_CCtxParams_registerSequenceProducer` | `extSeqProdFunc == NULL` | clears both func and state; never errors |\n\n## zstd_compress_literals.c\n\n| function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_noCompressLiterals` | `srcSize + flSize > dstCapacity`, `flSize = 1 + (srcSize>31) + (srcSize>4095)` | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_noCompressLiterals` | `flSize` not in `{1,2,3}` | `assert(0)` (debug-only); release: no header written, returns `srcSize+flSize` |\n| `ZSTD_compressRleLiteralsBlock` | `dstCapacity < 4` | `assert` (debug-only) — **no runtime check in release** |\n| `ZSTD_compressRleLiteralsBlock` | `!allBytesIdentical(src, srcSize)` | `assert` (debug-only) |\n| `ZSTD_compressLiterals` | `dstCapacity < lhSize+1`, `lhSize = 3 + (srcSize>=1 KB) + (srcSize>=16 KB)` | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressLiterals` | `disableLiteralCompression != 0` (`ZSTD_c_literalCompressionMode==ZSTD_ps_disable`) | falls back to `ZSTD_noCompressLiterals` (may yield `dstSize_tooSmall`) |\n| `ZSTD_compressLiterals` | `srcSize < ZSTD_minLiteralsToCompress(strategy, repeatMode)` | falls back to `ZSTD_noCompressLiterals` (not an error) |\n| `ZSTD_compressLiterals` | `cLitSize==0 \\|\\| cLitSize >= srcSize-minGain \\|\\| ERR_isError(cLitSize)` from HUF | falls back to `ZSTD_noCompressLiterals`; **a real HUF error code is swallowed** |\n| `ZSTD_compressLiterals` | `cLitSize==1 && (srcSize>=8 \\|\\| allBytesIdentical(src,srcSize))` | emits RLE literals block (not an error) |\n| `ZSTD_compressLiterals` | `lhSize` not in `{3,4,5}` | `assert(0)` (debug-only) |\n\n## zstd_compress_sequences.c\n\n| function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_fseBitCost` | `ZSTD_getFSEMaxSymbolValue(ctable) < max` (repeat CTable can't represent all symbols) | `ZSTD_error_GENERIC` (used as an \"infinite cost\" sentinel by callers) |\n| `ZSTD_fseBitCost` | `count[s]!=0 && bitCost >= ((tableLog+1)<<8)` (symbol has probability 0 in repeat table) | `ZSTD_error_GENERIC` (sentinel) |\n| `ZSTD_NCountCost` | `FSE_normalizeCount()` fails (`max > MaxSeq`, bad `tableLog`, `nbSeq==1`) | propagated FSE error (`ZSTD_error_GENERIC` / `maxSymbolValue_tooLarge` / `tableLog_tooLarge`) |\n| `ZSTD_NCountCost` | `FSE_writeNCount()` fails | propagated (`ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` / `GENERIC`) |\n| `ZSTD_selectEncodingType` | `!isDefaultAllowed` | `basicCost = ERROR(GENERIC)` used as \"infinite cost\", not returned |\n| `ZSTD_selectEncodingType` | `*repeatMode == FSE_repeat_none` | `repeatCost = ERROR(GENERIC)` used as \"infinite cost\", not returned |\n| `ZSTD_buildCTable(set_rle)` | `FSE_buildCTable_rle()` fails | propagated FSE error (`ZSTD_error_GENERIC`) |\n| `ZSTD_buildCTable(set_rle)` | `dstCapacity == 0` | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_buildCTable(set_repeat)` / `(set_basic)` | success | `0` — \"0 bytes written\", **not** a failure sentinel |\n| `ZSTD_buildCTable(set_basic)` | `FSE_buildCTable_wksp()` fails (wksp too small) | propagated (`tableLog_tooLarge` / `GENERIC` / `maxSymbolValue_tooLarge`) |\n| `ZSTD_buildCTable(set_compressed)` | `FSE_normalizeCount()` fails | propagated FSE error |\n| `ZSTD_buildCTable(set_compressed)` | `FSE_writeNCount(op, oend-op, ...)` fails (not enough dst for the count header) | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_buildCTable(set_compressed)` | `FSE_buildCTable_wksp()` fails | propagated FSE error |\n| `ZSTD_buildCTable` | `type` not a valid `SymbolEncodingType_e` | `assert(0)` + `ZSTD_error_GENERIC` |\n| `ZSTD_encodeSequences` / `_body` | `BIT_initCStream()` fails, i.e. `dstCapacity < sizeof(size_t)` (8) | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_encodeSequences` / `_body` | `BIT_closeCStream() == 0` (bitstream overflowed `dst`) | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_encodeSequences` / `_body` | `nbSeq == 0` | **no check** — `mlCodeTable[nbSeq-1]` underflows; caller must guarantee `nbSeq>=1` |\n\n## zstd_compress_superblock.c (only reachable with `ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize != 0`)\n\n| function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_literal` | `litSize==0 \\|\\| hType==set_basic` | delegates to `ZSTD_noCompressLiterals` (may yield `dstSize_tooSmall`) |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_literal` | `hType==set_rle` | delegates to `ZSTD_compressRleLiteralsBlock` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_literal` | `cSize==0 \\|\\| ERR_isError(cSize)` from `HUF_compress{1,4}X_usingCTable` | `0` — \"cannot compress\"; **a real HUF error code is swallowed into 0** |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_literal` | `!writeEntropy && cLitSize >= litSize` (expanded) | falls back to `ZSTD_noCompressLiterals` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_literal` | `lhSize < 3 + (cLitSize>=1 KB) + (cLitSize>=16 KB)` (guessed header too small) | falls back to `ZSTD_noCompressLiterals` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_literal` | `lhSize` not in `{3,4,5}` | `assert(0)` (debug-only) |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_sequences` | `(oend-op) < 3+1` (no room for nbSeq field + seqHead) | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_sequences` | `ZSTD_encodeSequences()` fails | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall`, propagated |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_sequences` | `writeEntropy && lastCountSize && lastCountSize+bitstreamSize < 4` (zstd ≤1.3.4 decoder-bug workaround) | `0` — \"cannot compress, emit uncompressed\" |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_sequences` | `op-seqHead < 4` (zstd ≤1.4.0 decoder-bug workaround) | `0` — \"cannot compress, emit uncompressed\" |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock` | `cLitSize == 0` or `cSeqSize == 0` | `0` — \"failed to compress\" |\n| `ZSTD_estimateSubBlockSize_literal` | `ZSTD_isError(HIST_count_wksp(...))` (wksp too small) | `litSize` — degraded estimate, **error swallowed** |\n| `ZSTD_estimateSubBlockSize_symbolType` | `type==set_basic && max > defaultMax`, or `ZSTD_fseBitCost` fails | `nbSeq * 10` — pessimistic fallback, **error swallowed** |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_multi` | `ebs.estBlockSize > srcSize` (superblock estimated incompressible) | `0` → caller emits one uncompressed block |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_multi` | `ZSTD_compressSubBlock()` fails on any sub-block | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall`, propagated |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_multi` | `!(cSize>0 && cSize<decompressedSize)` for a sub-block | sub-block not committed, coalesced with the next (not an error) |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_multi` | `writeSeqEntropy && ZSTD_needSequenceEntropyTables(...)` still true at the end (entropy tables never emitted) | `0` — caller must emit an uncompressed block |\n| `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_multi` | trailing raw bytes and `ZSTD_noCompressBlock()` fails | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` |\n| `ZSTD_compressSuperBlock` | `ZSTD_buildBlockEntropyStats()` fails (tmpWkspSize too small, FSE/HUF failure) | propagated (`GENERIC` / `dstSize_tooSmall` / `memory_allocation`) |\n| `ZSTD_compressSuperBlock` | `ZSTD_compressSubBlock_multi()` returns 0 | `0` → `ZSTD_compressBlock_targetCBlockSize_body` falls back to `ZSTD_noCompressBlock` |\n| `ZSTD_compressBlock_targetCBlockSize_body` | superblock cSize `== ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)`, or `0`, or `>= maxCSize + ZSTD_blockHeaderSize` | falls back to `ZSTD_noCompressBlock` → `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` if `dstCapacity < srcSize+3` |\n\n## zstd_ldm.c (only reachable with `ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching == ZSTD_ps_enable`)\n\n| function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences_internal` | `rawSeqStore->size == rawSeqStore->capacity` (out of LDM sequence storage) | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` — the only real error return in this file |\n| `ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences` | inner `ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences_internal()` errors | `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall`, propagated |\n| `ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences_internal` | `srcSize < params->minMatchLength` | returns `srcSize` (a