{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"af90496280bfd4004","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01CQNJLoWpmXh68HuwsBfzim","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-KufEFj-translated-rust/f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5/tasks/af90496280bfd4004.output","summary":"Done. Wrote `/tmp/err_compress.md`.\n\n## What was done\n\nRead all six requested C files (plus `zstd.h`, `zstd_errors.h`, `zstd_compress_internal.h`, `zstd_internal.h`, `clevels.h`, `zstdmt_compress.h`, and `zstd_decompress.c` for the `ZSTD_d_*` bounds) and enumerated every distinct rejection path. Read-only — no C source was touched.\n\n**414 table rows total:**\n\n| section | rows |\n|---|---|\n| `zstd_compress.c` (public API surface) | 254 |\n| `zstd_compress_literals.c` | 10 |\n| `zstd_compress_sequences.c` | 17 |\n| `zstd_compress_superblock.c` | 21 |\n| `zstd_ldm.c` | 9 |\n| `zstdmt_compress.c` | 54 |\n| `## BOUNDS TABLE` (41 `ZSTD_c_*` + 8 `ZSTD_d_*`) | 49 |\n\n## Key findings a Rust port must not get wrong\n\n- **Clamp vs. error is inconsistent and per-parameter.** `compressionLevel`, `nbWorkers`, `jobSize`, `overlapLog`, `rsyncable` *clamp silently* via `ZSTD_cParam_clampBounds`; everything else *errors* with `parameter_outOfBound` via `BOUNDCHECK`. `targetCBlockSize` does both (raises to 1340, then bound-checks). `contentSizeFlag`, `checksumFlag`, `dictIDFlag`, `forceMaxWindow`, `enableDedicatedDictSearch` have **no check at all** despite advertising bounds 0..1.\n- **`ZSTD_c_rsyncable` is clamped using `ZSTD_c_overlapLog` bounds** (`[0,9]`, not `[0,1]`) — a real quirk in `zstd_compress.c:905`.\n- **`value == 0` escapes BOUNDCHECK** for `windowLog`/`hashLog`/`chainLog`/`searchLog`/`minMatch`/`strategy`/`ldm*`/`srcSizeHint`/`maxBlockSize` (means \"default\"), but **not** for `targetLength`. Conversely `ZSTD_checkCParams` rejects `strategy==0` where `setParameter` accepts it.\n- **Errors deliberately swallowed** (porting these as `Err` changes behavior): `zstd_compress_literals.c:188` and `zstd_compress_superblock.c:83-86` turn HUF error codes into \"incompressible\"; `zstd_compress.c:3026` turns `dstSize_tooSmall` into `0`; superblock `:321`/`:356` turn errors into fallback size estimates; `zstdmt_compress.c:605` discards an LDM error via `(void)error`.\n- **`ERROR(GENERIC)` used as a numeric \"infinite cost\" sentinel**, not control flow: `zstd_compress_sequences.c:206,207`, `zstd_compress_superblock.c:350`.\n- **`0` is overloaded**: success/\"0 bytes written\" in `zstd_compress_sequences.c:263,266` and `ZSTDMT_createCompressionJob` (back-pressure), but *failure* in `zstd_compress_superblock.c:85,234,251,285,296,532,637`.\n- **MT dict/cdict conflict and buffer-validity are assert-only**, not error returns (`zstdmt_compress.c:1260,1861,1862`). MT error ordering in `ZSTDMT_initCStream_internal` is: resize → CDict #1 (dead work, but observable error) → roundBuff malloc → CDict #2 → serialState_reset.\n- `nbWorkers` too large is never an error (clamped twice); only `0` makes `ZSTDMT_createCCtx_advanced_internal` return NULL.\n- The whole compress side emits only **`memory_allocation`** and **`stage_wrong`** from `zstdmt_compress.c`, and only **`dstSize_tooSmall`** + **`GENERIC`** from the four auxiliary files; `dstBuffer_null` and `noForwardProgress_*` are never used on the compression side.","usage":{"total_tokens":267542,"tool_uses":36,"duration_ms":547810},"uuid":"70609835-ba0e-4cde-9575-2558fc0d8932","session_id":"f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5"}
