 `nbTrainSamples < 5`; splitPoint forced to 1.0 ⇒ `nbSamples < 5` | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover` (`COVER_ctx_init`) | `nbTestSamples < 1` (with splitPoint 1.0 equivalent to `nbSamples == 0`) | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover` (`COVER_ctx_init`) | `malloc` of `suffix` / `dmerAt` (`suffixSize * 4` each) or `offsets` (`(nbSamples+1)*8`) fails | `ERROR(memory_allocation)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover` | `COVER_map_init(&activeDmers, k-d+1)` malloc fails (allocates `2^(highbit32(k-d+1)+2)` pairs) | `ERROR(memory_allocation)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover` | `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary` on the built content fails | forwarded (`dstSize_tooSmall` / `dictionaryCreation_failed` / `memory_allocation` / entropy errors) |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | `parameters->splitPoint > 1.0` (`<= 0.0` is silently defaulted to `COVER_DEFAULT_SPLITPOINT` 1.0, so that half is dead) | `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | `kMinK < kMaxD`: `k != 0 && k < (d==0 ? 8 : d)`, or `k == 0 && d > 50` | `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | `kMaxK < kMinK` (unreachable: equal when `k!=0`, `2000 > 50` when `k==0`) | `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | `nbSamples == 0` | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | `dictBufferCapacity < ZDICT_DICTSIZE_MIN` (< 256) | `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | `nbThreads > 1` and `POOL_create(nbThreads, 1)` returns NULL | `ERROR(memory_allocation)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | `COVER_ctx_init` fails for the first `d` tried (see ctx_init rows; with default splitPoint 1.0, `nbSamples < 5`) | that error forwarded |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | `malloc(sizeof(COVER_tryParameters_data_t))` fails | `ERROR(memory_allocation)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | per-iteration `!COVER_checkParameters(data->parameters, dictBufferCapacity)` (e.g. `k > dictBufferCapacity`, `d > k`) | iteration silently `continue`d — no error returned |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | all iterations skipped or all failed ⇒ `best.compressedSize` remains its init value `(size_t)-1` | returns `(size_t)-1`, which `ZSTD_isError` reports true, `ZSTD_getErrorCode` == `ZSTD_error_GENERIC` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover` | `COVER_best_finish` could not `malloc(dictSize)` for the winner | `best.compressedSize = ERROR(GENERIC)` → returned |\n| `COVER_selectDict` | `malloc(dictBufferCapacity)` for `largestDictbuffer` or `candidateDictBuffer` fails | `COVER_dictSelectionError(dictContentSize)` (dictContent = NULL ⇒ `COVER_dictSelectionIsError` = 1) |\n| `COVER_selectDict` | `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary` fails (largest or a shrink candidate) | `COVER_dictSelectionError(thatError)` |\n| `COVER_selectDict` | `COVER_checkTotalCompressedSize` fails | `COVER_dictSelectionError(thatError)` |\n| `COVER_checkTotalCompressedSize` | `malloc(dstCapacity)` / `ZSTD_createCCtx` / `ZSTD_createCDict` fails | `ERROR(GENERIC)` (the initial value of `totalCompressedSize`) |\n| `COVER_checkTotalCompressedSize` | any `ZSTD_compress_usingCDict` returns an error | that error |\n| `COVER_dictSelectionIsError(sel)` | `ZSTD_isError(sel.totalCompressedSize)` **or** `sel.dictContent == NULL` | returns `1` |\n| `COVER_best_init/wait/destroy/start/finish` | `best == NULL` | no-op, no error |\n| `COVER_computeEpochs(maxDictSize, nbDmers, k, passes)` | `k == 0` or `passes == 0` (division `maxDictSize/k/passes`) | division by zero (UB); `k==0` is filtered by `COVER_checkParameters` |\n| `COVER_computeEpochs` | `nbDmers == 0` and `k*10 > 0` ⇒ `epochs.size = 0` then `nbDmers / epochs.size` | division by zero (UB); filtered upstream by `COVER_ctx_init` |\n| `COVER_sum(samplesSizes, nbSamples)` | total exceeds `SIZE_MAX` | silent `size_t` wraparound, no check |\n| `COVER_warnOnSmallCorpus` | `nbDmers / maxDictSize < 10` | prints a level-1 warning only; **not** an error |\n| `COVER_map_init(map, size)` | `malloc(2^(highbit32(size)+2) * 8)` fails | returns `0`; caller maps this to `ERROR(memory_allocation)` |\n| `COVER_map_at` | map is full (load factor >= 1) | `COVER_map_index` loops forever (documented: \"the map must be large enough\") |\n| **GROUP B — dictBuilder/fastcover.c** | | |\n| `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` | `parameters.d == 0` | returns `0` (invalid) |\n| `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` | `parameters.k == 0` | returns `0` (invalid) |\n| `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` | `parameters.d != 6 && parameters.d != 8` (e.g. 4, 5, 7, 16) | returns `0` (invalid) — **d must be exactly 6 or 8** |\n| `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` | `parameters.k > maxDictSize` | returns `0` (invalid) |\n| `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` | `parameters.d > parameters.k` | returns `0` (invalid) |\n| `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` | `f > FASTCOVER_MAX_F` (> 31) or `f == 0` | returns `0` (invalid); accepted range is `1..31` |\n| `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` | `parameters.splitPoint <= 0.0` or `> 1.0` | returns `0` (invalid); accepted range is `(0.0, 1.0]` |\n| `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` | `accel > 10` or `accel == 0` | returns `0` (invalid); accepted range is `1..10` |\n| `FASTCOVER_checkParameters` | any `steps`, any `nbThreads`, any `shrinkDict` / `shrinkDictMaxRegression` | **not validated here** |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `!FASTCOVER_checkParameters(coverParams, dictBufferCapacity, f, accel)` after `f=0→20`, `accel=0→1`, `splitPoint:=1.0`; reachable causes: `d==0`, `d∉{6,8}`, `k==0`, `k > dictBufferCapacity`, `d > k`, `f > 31` | `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `nbSamples == 0` | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `dictBufferCapacity < ZDICT_DICTSIZE_MIN` (< 256) | `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` (`FASTCOVER_ctx_init`) | `COVER_sum(...) < MAX(d, 8)` | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` (`FASTCOVER_ctx_init`) | `COVER_sum(...) >= FASTCOVER_MAX_SAMPLES_SIZE` (`>= 4294967295` on 64-bit, `>= 1073741824` on 32-bit) | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` (`FASTCOVER_ctx_init`) | `nbTrainSamples < 5`; splitPoint forced 1.0 ⇒ `nbSamples < 5` | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` (`FASTCOVER_ctx_init`) | `nbTestSamples < 1` | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` (`FASTCOVER_ctx_init`) | `calloc(nbSamples+1, sizeof(size_t))` fails | `ERROR(memory_allocation)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` (`FASTCOVER_ctx_init`) | `calloc(1<<f, sizeof(U32))` fails (2^f * 4 bytes; 4 MiB at f=20, 8 GiB at f=31) | `ERROR(memory_allocation)` |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `calloc(1<<f, sizeof(U16))` for `segmentFreqs` fails — return value is **never checked** | NULL deref in `FASTCOVER_selectSegment` (crash, no error code) |\n| `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary` fails | forwarded |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `parameters->splitPoint > 1.0` (`<= 0.0` silently defaulted to `FASTCOVER_DEFAULT_SPLITPOINT` 0.75) | `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `accel > FASTCOVER_MAX_ACCEL` (> 10); `accel == 0` is defaulted to 1 first so that half is dead | `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `kMinK < kMaxD`: `k != 0 && k < (d==0 ? 8 : d)`, or `k == 0 && d > 50` | `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `kMaxK < kMinK` (unreachable) | `ERROR(parameter_outOfBound)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `nbSamples == 0` | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `dictBufferCapacity < ZDICT_DICTSIZE_MIN` (< 256) | `ERROR(dstSize_tooSmall)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `nbThreads > 1` and `POOL_create(nbThreads, 1)` returns NULL | `ERROR(memory_allocation)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `FASTCOVER_ctx_init` fails; with default splitPoint 0.75, `(unsigned)(nbSamples*0.75) < 5` ⇒ `nbSamples <= 6` | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | with `splitPoint < 1.0`, `nbSamples - (unsigned)(nbSamples*splitPoint) < 1` | `ERROR(srcSize_wrong)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | `malloc(sizeof(FASTCOVER_tryParameters_data_t))` fails | `ERROR(memory_allocation)` |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | per-iteration `!FASTCOVER_checkParameters(...)` (e.g. `parameters->d` fixed to something not 6 or 8, or `k > dictBufferCapacity`) | iteration silently `continue`d |\n| `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` | all iterations skipped/failed ⇒ `best.compressedSize` remains `(size_t)-1` (e.g. caller sets `d = 7`) | returns `(size_t)-1` → `ZSTD_getErrorCode` == `ZSTD_error_GENERIC` |\n| `FASTCOVER_tryParameters` (worker) | `calloc(1<<f, sizeof(U16))`, `malloc(dictBufferCapacity)` or `malloc((1<<f)*sizeof(U32))` fails | `selection = COVER_dictSelectionError(ERROR(GENERIC))`; `best` not updated |\n| `FASTCOVER_tryParameters` (worker) | `COVER_dictSelectionIsError(selection)` | `best` not updated; overall optimize call ends with the `(size_t)-1` / `GENERIC` result |\n| **GROUP B — dictBuilder/divsufsort.c** | | |\n| `divsufsort(T, SA, n, openMP)` | `T == NULL` | returns `-1` |\n| `divsufsort` | `SA == NULL` | returns `-1` |\n| `divsufsort` | `n < 0` | returns `-1` |\n| `divsufsort` | `n == 0` | returns `0`, `SA` untouched (not an error) |\n| `divsufsort` | `n == 1` | returns `0`, `SA[0] = 0` |\n| `divsufsort` | `n == 2` | returns `0`, both entries written |\n| `divsufsort` | `malloc(BUCKET_A_SIZE*sizeof(int))` (1024 B) or `malloc(BUCKET_B_SIZE*sizeof(int))` (262144 B) fails | returns `-2`, `SA` left unsorted |\n| `divbwt(T, U, A, n, num_indexes, indexes, openMP)` | `T == NULL` | returns `-1` |\n| `divbwt` | `U == NULL` | returns `-1` |\n| `divbwt` | `n < 0` | returns `-1` |\n| `divbwt` | `n == 0` | returns `0` (not an error) |\n| `divbwt` | `n == 1` | returns `1`, `U[0] = T[0]` |\n| `divbwt` | `A == NULL` and `malloc((n+1)*sizeof(int))` fails, or either bucket malloc fails | returns `-2` |\n\n## ERROR STRING TABLE\n\nEvery case of `ERR_getErrorString(ERR_enum code)` in `c_src/src/common/error_private.c`.\nDirectly observable via `ZSTD_getErrorString(code)`, and via\n`ZSTD_getErrorName((size_t)-code)` / `FSE_getErrorName` / `HUF_getErrorName` / `ZDICT_getErrorName`.\nIf `ZSTD_STRIP_ERROR_STRINGS` is defined, *every* code returns `\"Error strings stripped\"`.\n\n| ZSTD_error_* | code | exact string returned by ERR_getErrorString |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_error_no_error` | 0 | `No error detected` |\n| `ZSTD_error_GENERIC` | 1 | `Error (generic)` |\n| `ZSTD_error_prefix_unknown` | 10 | `Unknown frame descriptor` |\n| `ZSTD_error_version_unsupported` | 12 | `Version not supported` |\n| `ZSTD_error_frameParameter_unsupported` | 14 | `Unsupported frame parameter` |\n| `ZSTD_error_frameParameter_windowTooLarge` | 16 | `Frame requires too much memory for decoding` |\n| `ZSTD_error_corruption_detected` | 20 | `Data corruption detected` |\n| `ZSTD_error_checksum_wrong` | 22 | `Restored data doesn't match checksum` |\n| `ZSTD_error_literals_headerWrong` | 24 | `Header of Literals' block doesn't respect format specification` |\n| `ZSTD_error_dictionary_corrupted` | 30 | `Dictionary is corrupted` |\n| `ZSTD_error_dictionary_wrong` | 32 | `Dictionary mismatch` |\n| `ZSTD_error_dictionaryCreation_failed` | 34 | `Cannot create Dictionary from provided samples` |\n| `ZSTD_error_parameter_unsupported` | 40 | `Unsupported parameter` |\n| `ZSTD_error_parameter_combination_unsupported` | 41 | `Unsupported combination of parameters` |\n| `ZSTD_error_parameter_outOfBound` | 42 | `Parameter is out of bound` |\n| `ZSTD_error_tableLog_tooLarge` | 44 | `tableLog requires too much memory : unsupported` |\n| `ZSTD_error_maxSymbolValue_tooLarge` | 46 | `Unsupported max Symbol Value : too large` |\n| `ZSTD_error_maxSymbolValue_tooSmall` | 48 | `Specified maxSymbolValue is too small` |\n| `ZSTD_error_cannotProduce_uncompressedBlock` | 49 | `This mode cannot generate an uncompressed block` |\n| `ZSTD_error_stabilityCondition_notRespected` | 50 | `pledged buffer stability condition is not respected` |\n| `ZSTD_error_stage_wrong` | 60 | `Operation not authorized at current processing stage` |\n| `ZSTD_error_init_missing` | 62 | `Context should be init first` |\n| `ZSTD_error_memory_allocation` | 64 | `Allocation error : not enough memory` |\n| `ZSTD_error_workSpace_tooSmall` | 66 | `workSpace buffer is not large enough` |\n| `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall` | 70 | `Destination buffer is too small` |\n| `ZSTD_error_srcSize_wrong` | 72 | `Src size is incorrect` |\n| `ZSTD_error_dstBuffer_null` | 74 | `Operation on NULL destination buffer` |\n| `ZSTD_error_noForwardProgress_destFull` | 80 | `Operation made no progress over multiple calls, due to output buffer being full` |\n| `ZSTD_error_noForwardProgress_inputEmpty` | 82 | `Operation made no progress over multiple calls, due to input being empty` |\n| `ZSTD_error_frameIndex_tooLarge` | 100 | `Frame index is too large` |\n| `ZSTD_error_seekableIO` | 102 | `An I/O error occurred when reading/seeking` |\n| `ZSTD_error_dstBuffer_wrong` | 104 | `Destination buffer is wrong` |\n| `ZSTD_error_srcBuffer_wrong` | 105 | `Source buffer is wrong` |\n| `ZSTD_error_sequenceProducer_failed` | 106 | `Block-level external sequence producer returned an error code` |\n| `ZSTD_error_externalSequences_invalid` | 107 | `External sequences are not valid` |\n| `ZSTD_error_maxCode` | 120 | `Unspecified error code` (falls into `default`) |\n| any other value (2..9, 11, 13, 15, 17..19, 21, 23, 25..29, 31, 33, 35..39, 43, 45, 47, 51..59, 61, 63, 65, 67..69, 71, 73, 75..79, 81, 83..99, 101, 103, 108..119, >120) | — | `Unspecified error code` |\n\nNote on the boundary: `ERR_isError(code)` is `code > (size_t)-120`. So `(size_t)-120` itself\n(== `ERROR(maxCode)`) is *not* an error, while `(size_t)-119` .. `(size_t)-1` all are.\n`(size_t)-1` (the `COVER_best_t` sentinel) decodes to code `1` == `GENERIC` == `\"Error (generic)\"`.\n\n## ENTROPY/DICT LIMIT CONSTANTS\n\n| macro | value |\n|---|---|\n| `FSE_MAX_MEMORY_USAGE` | `14` |\n| `FSE_DEFAULT_MEMORY_USAGE` | `13` |\n| `FSE_MAX_TABLELOG` | `FSE_MAX_MEMORY_USAGE-2` = **12** |\n| `FSE_DEFAULT_TABLELOG` | `FSE_DEFAULT_MEMORY_USAGE-2` = **11** |\n| `FSE_MIN_TABLELOG` | **5** |\n| `FSE_TABLELOG_ABSOLUTE_MAX` | **15** |\n| `FSE_MAX_SYMBOL_VALUE` | **255** |\n| `FSE_MAX_TABLESIZE` | `1U<<12` = **4096** |\n| `FSE_MAXTABLESIZE_MASK` | **4095** |\n| `FSE_NCOUNTBOUND` | **512** |\n| `FSE_BLOCKBOUND(size)` | `size + (size>>7) + 4 + sizeof(size_t)` (= `size + (size>>7) + 12` on 64-bit) |\n| `FSE_COMPRESSBOUND(size)` | `512 + size + (size>>7) + 4 + sizeof(size_t)` |\n| `FSE_TABLESTEP(tableSize)` | `(tableSize>>1) + (tableSize>>3) + 3` |\n| `FSE_CTABLE_SIZE_U32(maxTableLog, maxSV)` | `1 + (1<<(maxTableLog-1)) + ((maxSV+1)*2)` |\n| `FSE_DTABLE_SIZE_U32(maxTableLog)` | `1 + (1<<maxTableLog)` |\n| `FSE_BUILD_CTABLE_WORKSPACE_SIZE_U32(maxSV, tableLog)` | `((maxSV+2) + (1ull<<tableLog))/2 + 2` (= **2178** U32 for 255/12) |\n| `FSE_BUILD_CTABLE_WORKSPACE_SIZE(maxSV, tableLog)` | `4 *` the above (= **8712** bytes for 255/12) |\n| `FSE_BUILD_DTABLE_WKSP_SIZE(maxTableLog, maxSV)` | `2*(maxSV+1) + (1ULL<<maxTableLog) + 8` (= **4616** bytes for 12/255) |\n| `FSE_DECOMPRESS_WKSP_SIZE_U32(maxTableLog, maxSV)` | `FSE_DTABLE_SIZE_U32(maxTableLog) + 1 + FSE_BUILD_DTABLE_WKSP_SIZE_U32(maxTableLog,maxSV) + 128 + 1` |\n| `sizeof(FSE_DecompressWksp)` | `2 * (FSE_MAX_SYMBOL_VALUE+1)` = **512** bytes (the `wkspSize` floor that yields `GENERIC`) |\n| `HUF_BLOCKSIZE_MAX` | `128 * 1024` = **131072** |\n| `HUF_WORKSPACE_SIZE` | `(8<<10) + 512` = **8704** |\n| `HUF_WORKSPACE_SIZE_U64` | **1088** |\n| `HUF_WORKSPACE_MAX_ALIGNMENT` | **8** |\n| `HUF_TABLELOG_M