aps to `dictSize + 499`.\nSo \"unknown srcSize + a dictionary\" picks the table from `dictSize+499`, i.e. a *small*\ntable (tableID 3 for any dict under ~16 KB), not table 0. Reproduce exactly.\n\n`ZSTD_CParamMode_e` (`zstd_compress_internal.h:558-576`): `ZSTD_cpm_noAttachDict`,\n`ZSTD_cpm_attachDict`, `ZSTD_cpm_createCDict`, `ZSTD_cpm_unknown`.\n\n### Row (level) selection + special handling of 0 and negatives\n\n```c\nif (compressionLevel == 0)                    row = ZSTD_CLEVEL_DEFAULT;   /* == 3 */\nelse if (compressionLevel < 0)                row = 0;                     /* the \"base\" row */\nelse if (compressionLevel > ZSTD_MAX_CLEVEL)  row = ZSTD_MAX_CLEVEL;       /* clamp to 22 */\nelse                                          row = compressionLevel;\n...\nif (compressionLevel < 0) {\n    int const clampedCompressionLevel = MAX(ZSTD_minCLevel(), compressionLevel);\n    cp.targetLength = (unsigned)(-clampedCompressionLevel);\n}\nreturn ZSTD_adjustCParams_internal(cp, srcSizeHint, dictSize, mode, ZSTD_ps_auto);\n```\n\n* Level **0** is *not* row 0 — it maps to row 3 (the default level). Row 0 is only reachable\n  through negative levels.\n* Row 0 is always `strategy = ZSTD_fast` and `targetLength = 1` in the table, but the\n  `targetLength` is overwritten by `-level` for negative levels: `-1 -> 1`, `-5 -> 5`,\n  `-1000 -> 1000`, `-131072 -> 131072`; anything below `-131072` clamps to `131072`.\n* Interaction: negative levels give `strategy == ZSTD_fast && targetLength > 0`, and\n  `ZSTD_literalsCompressionIsDisabled()` (`zstd_compress_internal.h:685-697`) returns 1 for\n  `ZSTD_ps_auto` under exactly that condition => **negative levels emit uncompressed\n  literals by default**. Level 1 (targetLength 0) does not.\n* `ZSTD_getCParams(level, srcSizeHint, dictSize)` / `ZSTD_getParams(...)` public wrappers map\n  `srcSizeHint == 0` to `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN` (`zstd_compress.c:7787-7791`, `:7813-7817`),\n  whereas the internal `srcSizeHint == 0` means literally zero. Two distinct behaviours.\n* `ZSTD_c_srcSizeHint` feeds in via `ZSTD_getCParamsFromCCtxParams` (`:1641-1644`) only when\n  the real srcSizeHint is `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN`.\n* `ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching == ZSTD_ps_enable` overrides\n  `cParams.windowLog = ZSTD_LDM_DEFAULT_WINDOW_LOG` **before** `ZSTD_overrideCParams`\n  (`:1646`), so an explicit `ZSTD_c_windowLog` still wins.\n* `ZSTD_overrideCParams` (`:1624-1635`) treats **0 as \"not set\"** for every cParam, so 0 can\n  never be pinned explicitly.\n\n### `ZSTD_adjustCParams_internal` clamps (`zstd_compress.c:1477-1608`)\n\n`minSrcSize = 513`, `maxWindowResize = 1ULL << (ZSTD_WINDOWLOG_MAX-1)` = 2^30 on 64-bit.\n\n1. mode switch: `ZSTD_cpm_createCDict` + `dictSize && srcSize==UNKNOWN` -> `srcSize = 513`;\n   `ZSTD_cpm_attachDict` -> `dictSize = 0`; `unknown`/`noAttachDict` -> unchanged.\n2. If `srcSize <= 2^30 && dictSize <= 2^30`: `tSize = srcSize+dictSize`;\n   `srcLog = (tSize < (1<<ZSTD_HASHLOG_MIN=6)) ? 6 : highbit32(tSize-1)+1`;\n   `windowLog = MIN(windowLog, srcLog)`.\n3. If `srcSize != UNKNOWN`: `dictAndWindowLog = ZSTD_dictAndWindowLog(windowLog, srcSize, dictSize)`;\n   `hashLog = MIN(hashLog, dictAndWindowLog+1)`;\n   `cycleLog = ZSTD_cycleLog(chainLog, strategy) = chainLog - (strategy >= ZSTD_btlazy2)`;\n   `if (cycleLog > dictAndWindowLog) chainLog -= (cycleLog - dictAndWindowLog)`.\n4. `windowLog = MAX(windowLog, ZSTD_WINDOWLOG_ABSOLUTEMIN=10)`.\n5. `mode == ZSTD_cpm_createCDict && ZSTD_CDictIndicesAreTagged(cPar)` (i.e. strategy\n   `fast` or `dfast`) -> `hashLog, chainLog <= 32 - ZSTD_SHORT_CACHE_TAG_BITS`.\n6. row-MF hashLog clamp (see AXIS 1 item 5), with `auto` optimistically = enable.\n\n`ZSTD_dictAndWindowLog` (`:1439-1462`): `dictSize==0` -> unchanged;\n`windowSize >= dictSize+srcSize` -> unchanged; `dictSize+windowSize >= 2^ZSTD_WINDOWLOG_MAX`\n-> `ZSTD_WINDOWLOG_MAX`; else `highbit32((U32)(dictSize+windowSize)-1)+1`.\n\nPublic `ZSTD_adjustCParams(cPar, srcSize, dictSize)` clamps first and maps `srcSize==0` to\n`UNKNOWN` (`:7611-7618` region), unlike the internal.\n\n---\n\n## AXIS 3 PARAMS\n\nParameter bounds live in `ZSTD_cParam_getBounds` (`zstd_compress.c:420-637`).\nConstant values from `zstd.h:1263-1308` (LE 64-bit): `ZSTD_WINDOWLOG_MIN=10`,\n`ZSTD_WINDOWLOG_MAX=31`, `ZSTD_HASHLOG_MIN=6`, `ZSTD_HASHLOG_MAX=30`,\n`ZSTD_CHAINLOG_MIN=6`, `ZSTD_CHAINLOG_MAX=30`, `ZSTD_SEARCHLOG_MIN=1`,\n`ZSTD_SEARCHLOG_MAX=30`, `ZSTD_MINMATCH_MIN=3`, `ZSTD_MINMATCH_MAX=7`,\n`ZSTD_TARGETLENGTH_MIN=0`, `ZSTD_TARGETLENGTH_MAX=131072`,\n`ZSTD_TARGETCBLOCKSIZE_MIN=1340`, `ZSTD_TARGETCBLOCKSIZE_MAX=131072`,\n`ZSTD_SRCSIZEHINT_MIN=0`, `ZSTD_SRCSIZEHINT_MAX=INT_MAX`,\n`ZSTD_LDM_MINMATCH_MIN=4`, `ZSTD_LDM_MINMATCH_MAX=4096`,\n`ZSTD_LDM_BUCKETSIZELOG_MIN=1`, `ZSTD_LDM_BUCKETSIZELOG_MAX=8`,\n`ZSTD_LDM_HASHRATELOG_MIN=0`, `ZSTD_LDM_HASHRATELOG_MAX=25`,\n`ZSTD_OVERLAPLOG_MIN=0`, `ZSTD_OVERLAPLOG_MAX=9`,\n`ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX_MIN=1024`, `ZSTD_BLOCKSPLITTER_LEVEL_MAX=6`.\n\nSwitch enum: `ZSTD_ps_auto=0`, `ZSTD_ps_enable=1`, `ZSTD_ps_disable=2` (`zstd.h:1456-1458`).\n\n### Stable parameters\n\n| ZSTD_c_* name | enum value | distinct values to exercise | affects output how |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_c_compressionLevel` | 100 | `-131072, -1000, -5, -1, 0, 1, 3, 5, 9, 12, 13, 16, 17, 18, 19, 22, 99(clamped)` | picks clevels.h row; `<0` sets `targetLength=-level` on the fast base row and turns literal compression off in `auto` mode; `0`->3; `>22`->22 |\n| `ZSTD_c_windowLog` | 101 | `0(default), 10(MIN), 14, 15, 17, 18, 27(LIMIT_DEFAULT), 31(MAX)` | back-reference distance; header `windowLogByte`; row-MF auto trigger (`>14`); LDM auto trigger (`>=27`); block splitter auto trigger (`>=17`); decoder-side window budget |\n| `ZSTD_c_hashLog` | 102 | `0, 6(MIN), 12, 17, 24, 30(MAX)` | match-finder table size -> which matches are found -> different sequences |\n| `ZSTD_c_chainLog` | 103 | `0, 6(MIN), 16, 24, 30(MAX)` | chain/bt table size; no effect for `ZSTD_fast`; secondary table for `dfast`; drives `ZSTD_cycleLog` and overflow-correction frequency |\n| `ZSTD_c_searchLog` | 104 | `0, 1(MIN), 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 30(MAX)` | nb search attempts; for row MF, `rowLog=BOUNDED(4,searchLog,6)` selects 16- vs 32- vs 64-entry rows (>=5 => 32-entry) — changes matches found |\n| `ZSTD_c_minMatch` | 105 | `0, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7` | mls; `<btopt` effective min is 4, `>fast` effective max is 6; `minMatch==3` also allocates hashLog3 (`h3Size`) in the CCtx |\n| `ZSTD_c_targetLength` | 106 | `0, 1, 8, 32, 64, 256, 999, 131072(MAX)` | for `btopt/btultra/btultra2`: \"good enough\" match length; for `fast`: match-sampling stride (`hasStep`); `>0` with `fast` disables literal compression in `auto` mode |\n| `ZSTD_c_strategy` | 107 | `0(default), 1..9` | see AXIS 1 |\n| `ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize` | 130 | `0(off), 1340(MIN), 2048, 8192, 65536, 131072(MAX)` | non-zero routes every block through `ZSTD_compressBlock_targetCBlockSize` -> `ZSTD_compressSuperBlock` (multiple sub-blocks per input block, own literal/seq splitting); also gates `ZSTD_generateSequences` (errors if non-zero) |\n| `ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching` | 160 | `ZSTD_ps_auto(0)`, `enable(1)`, `disable(2)` | `enable` forces `windowLog = ZSTD_LDM_DEFAULT_WINDOW_LOG` (unless pinned), runs `ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences` + `ZSTD_ldm_blockCompress` instead of a plain block compressor. `auto` = enable iff `strategy >= ZSTD_btopt && windowLog >= 27` |\n| `ZSTD_c_ldmHashLog` | 161 | `0(auto = windowLog-7)`, `6(MIN)`, `20`, `30(MAX)` | LDM table size -> which long matches are found |\n| `ZSTD_c_ldmMinMatch` | 162 | `0(default 64)`, `4(MIN)`, `32`, `64`, `4096(MAX)` | min LDM match length |\n| `ZSTD_c_ldmBucketSizeLog` | 163 | `0(default 3)`, `1(MIN)`, `3`, `8(MAX)` | LDM collision-resolution bucket size |\n| `ZSTD_c_ldmHashRateLog` | 164 | `0(auto = MAX(0, windowLog-ldmHashLog))`, `1`, `7`, `25(MAX)` | LDM insert/lookup stride |\n| `ZSTD_c_contentSizeFlag` | 200 | `0, 1(default)` | when 0: `fcsCode = 0` and `singleSegment = 0` in the frame header (no frame content size field at all) |\n| `ZSTD_c_checksumFlag` | 201 | `0(default), 1` | appends a 4-byte `XXH64(content) & 0xFFFFFFFF` at end of frame; sets FHD bit 2; incompatible with `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals` |\n| `ZSTD_c_dictIDFlag` | 202 | `0, 1(default)` | when 0 forces `dictIDSizeCode = 0` -> dictID omitted from header even with a dict |\n| `ZSTD_c_nbWorkers` | 400 | **only 0** — bounds `[0,0]`, non-zero returns `parameter_unsupported` | n/a in this build |\n| `ZSTD_c_jobSize` | 401 | **only 0** — non-zero returns `parameter_unsupported`; `ZSTD_CCtx_getParameter` also errors | n/a |\n| `ZSTD_c_overlapLog` | 402 | **only 0** — same | n/a |\n\n### Experimental parameters (require `ZSTD_STATIC_LINKING_ONLY`)\n\n| ZSTD_c_* name | enum value | distinct values to exercise | affects output how |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_c_rsyncable` | `experimentalParam1` = **500** | **only 0** (`parameter_unsupported` otherwise, MT-only) | n/a |\n| `ZSTD_c_format` | `experimentalParam2` = **10** | `ZSTD_f_zstd1(0)`, `ZSTD_f_zstd1_magicless(1)` | magicless omits the 4-byte `ZSTD_MAGICNUMBER`; `ZSTD_FRAMEHEADERSIZE_PREFIX` 5->1, `_MIN` 6->2. Decoder needs the matching `ZSTD_d_format`, and magicless disables legacy auto-dispatch (`zstd_decompress.c:740, 1090` gate on `format == ZSTD_f_zstd1`) |\n| `ZSTD_c_forceMaxWindow` | `experimentalParam3` = **1000** | `0(default), 1` | sets `params->forceWindow`; keeps back-refs `< windowSize` even into dict content; also **forbids dict attaching** (`ZSTD_shouldAttachDict` requires `!forceWindow`), so it flips `dictMatchState` -> `noDict`; sets `loadedDictEnd = 0` |\n| `ZSTD_c_forceAttachDict` | `experimentalParam4` = **1001** | `ZSTD_dictDefaultAttach(0)`, `ZSTD_dictForceAttach(1)`, `ZSTD_dictForceCopy(2)`, `ZSTD_dictForceLoad(3)` | picks attach (`dictMatchState`) vs copy (`noDict`) vs full reload (`noDict`, and skips `ZSTD_resetCCtx_usingCDict` entirely) — different match finders and different entropy-table starting state |\n| `ZSTD_c_literalCompressionMode` | `experimentalParam5` = **1002** | `ZSTD_ps_auto(0)`, `ZSTD_ps_enable(1)`, `ZSTD_ps_disable(2)` | `disable` forces `set_basic` (raw) literals sections always; `enable` always attempts Huffman; `auto` = disabled iff `strategy == ZSTD_fast && targetLength > 0` (i.e. negative levels) |\n| `ZSTD_c_srcSizeHint` | `experimentalParam7` = **1004** | `0(off), 1, 1024, 16384, 131072, 262144, 1<<20, INT_MAX` | substituted for an unknown srcSizeHint in `ZSTD_getCParamsFromCCtxParams` -> changes clevels tableID and every `adjustCParams` clamp. Does **not** appear in the frame header |\n| `ZSTD_c_enableDedicatedDictSearch` | `experimentalParam8` = **1005** | `0(default), 1` | with `ZSTD_createCDict_advanced2`: builds a DDS CDict (hashLog += `ZSTD_LAZY_DDSS_BUCKET_LOG`) and forces `dictMode = ZSTD_dedicatedDictSearch`; silently falls back to 0 if resolved strategy is outside `greedy..lazy2` |\n| `ZSTD_c_stableInBuffer` | `experimentalParam9` = **1006** | `ZSTD_bm_buffered(0)`, `ZSTD_bm_stable(1)` | `stable` skips the internal input buffer (`buffInSize = 0`), so blocks are cut at different boundaries than the buffered path -> **different block segmentation, different bytes**; caller must keep `ZSTD_inBuffer` identical across calls |\n| `ZSTD_c_stableOutBuffer` | `experimentalParam10` = **1007** | `ZSTD_bm_buffered(0)`, `ZSTD_bm_stable(1)` | `stable` skips the output buffer and lets `dstSize_tooSmall` propagate; changes when a block is emitted (`oSize >= ZSTD_compressBound(iSize) || outBufferMode == stable`) |\n| `ZSTD_c_blockDelimiters` | `experimentalParam11` = **1008** | `ZSTD_sf_noBlockDelimiters(0)`, `ZSTD_sf_explicitBlockDelimiters(1)` | interprets the `ZSTD_Sequence[]` array for `ZSTD_compressSequences`; `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals` **requires** `explicit` (else `frameParameter_unsupported`); `ZSTD_generateSequences` output shape |\n| `ZSTD_c_validateSequences` | `experimentalParam12` = **1009** | `0(default), 1` | validates externally supplied sequences before encoding; rejected by `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals` when 1 |\n| `ZSTD_c_blockSplitterLevel` | `experimentalParam20` = **1017** | `0(auto by strategy), 1(off/full 128KB blocks), 2, 3, 4, 5, 6(MAX)` | **pre**-splitter: `ZSTD_optimalBlockSize` -> `ZSTD_splitBlock`. `0` maps strategy->level via `splitLevels[] = {0,0,1,2,2,3,3,4,4,4}`; `1` = never split; `2..6` map to `splitLevel-2`. Only active when `srcSize >= 128 KB && blockSizeMax >= 128 KB && savings >= 3` |\n| `ZSTD_c_splitAfterSequences` (a.k.a. useBlockSplitter) | `experimentalParam13` = **1010** | `ZSTD_ps_auto(0)`, `enable(1)`, `disable(2)` | **post**-splitter: routes blocks through `ZSTD_compressBlock_splitBlock`, which re-partitions the seqStore. `auto` = enable iff `strategy >= ZSTD_btopt && windowLog >= 17` |\n| `ZSTD_c_useRowMatchFinder` | `experimentalParam14` = **1011** | `ZSTD_ps_auto(0)`, `enable(1)`, `disable(2)` | see AXIS 1 |\n| `ZSTD_c_deterministicRefPrefix` | `experimentalParam15` = **1012** | `0(default), 1` | `1` sets `ms->forceNonContiguous` after loading a dict/prefix, forcing the prefix into **extDict** mode regardless of memory layout -> selects the `*_extDict*` block compressors deterministically |\n| `ZSTD_c_prefetchCDictTables` | `experimentalParam16` = **1013** | `ZSTD_ps_auto(0)`, `enable(1)`, `disable(2)` | `PREFETCH_AREA` only, in `ZSTD_compressBlock_fast_dictMatchState` (`zstd_fast.c:527`) and `_doubleFast_dictMatchState` (`zstd_double_fast.c:368`). **No output change** — perf only; still worth one row to prove byte-identity |\n| `ZSTD_c_enableSeqProducerFallback` | `experimentalParam17` = **1014** | `0(default), 1` | with a registered external sequence producer, `1` falls back to the internal parser (re-running `ZSTD_selectBlockCompressor`) instead of erroring |\n| `ZSTD_c_maxBlockSize` | `experimentalParam18` = **1015** | `0(=default 131072)`, `1024(MIN)`, `4096`, `65536`, `131072(MAX)` | `ZSTD_resolveMaxBlockSize`; `blockSizeMax = MIN(maxBlockSize, 1<<windowLog)`; changes block segmentation and hence bytes; also `ZSTD_getBlockSize()` and the `ZSTD_compressBlock` srcSize limit; disables the pre-splitter when `< 128 KB` |\n| `ZSTD_c_repcodeResolution` / `ZSTD_c_searchForExternalRepcodes` | `experimentalParam19` = **1016** | `ZSTD_ps_auto(0)`, `enable(1)`, `disable(2)` | for external/explicit sequences: whether offsets are re-expressed as repcodes. `auto` = `disable` if `compressionLevel < 10` else `enable` (`ZSTD_resolveExternalRepcodeSearch`) — note it reads `compressionLevel`, so pinning cParams without a level changes the resolution |\n\nNot in the requested list but present and output-relevant: `ZSTD_CCtx_setCParams`,\n`ZSTD_CCtx_setFParams`, `ZSTD_CCtx_setParams` (bulk setters), and `ZSTD_c_experimentalParam6`\nwhich was retired (now `ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize` at 130).\n\n### Decompression-side parameters (`ZSTD_dParam_getBounds`, `zstd_decompress.c:1821-1859`)\n\n| ZSTD_d_* name | enum value | distinct values | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_d_windowLogMax` | 100 | `10(ZSTD_WINDOWLOG_ABSOLUTEMIN)`, `27(LIMIT_DEFAULT)`, `31(MAX)` | accept/refuse large-window frames; changes `ZSTD_decodingBufferSize_min` / `ZSTD_estimateDStreamSize` |\n| `ZSTD_d_format` | `d_experimentalParam1` = 1000 | `ZSTD_f_zstd1(0)`, `ZSTD_f_zstd1_magicless(1)` | must match `ZSTD_c_format`; magicless disables the legacy/skippable-frame paths |\n| `ZSTD_d_stableOutBuffer` | `d_experimentalParam2` = 1001 | `ZSTD_bm_buffered(0)`, `ZSTD_bm_stable(1)` | decompress directly into the caller buffer (no internal window buffer) |\n| `ZSTD_d_forceIgnoreChecksum` | `d_experimentalParam3` = 1002 | `ZSTD_d_validateChecksum(0)`, `ZSTD_d_ignoreChecksum(1)` | skip the trailing xxh64 check |\n| `ZSTD_d_refMultipleDDicts` | `d_experimentalParam4` = 1003 | `ZSTD_rmd_refSingleDDict(0)`, `ZSTD_rmd_refMultipleDDicts(1)` | accumulate DDicts in a hash set and select per-frame by dictID |\n| `ZSTD_d_disableHuffmanAssembly` | `d_experimentalParam5` = 1004 | `0, 1` | no-op for output in this build (no ASM compiled) |\n| `ZSTD_d_maxBlockSize` | `d_experimentalParam6` = 1005 | `1024(MIN)`, `65536`, `131072(MAX)` | max accepted block size; shrinks the allocated window buffer |\n\n---\n\n## AXIS 4 ENTRY POINTS\n\nAll names below are verified present in the exported symbol table (615 symbols,\n`SYMBOLS.md`). Context lifecycle helpers are listed once at the end of each group.\n\n### (a) simple one-shot\n`ZSTD_compress`, `ZSTD_compressCCtx`, `ZSTD_decompress`, `ZSTD_decompressDCtx`,\n`ZSTD_compressBound`, `ZSTD_getDecompressedSize` (deprecated), `ZSTD_versionNumber`,\n`ZSTD_versionString`, `ZSTD_isError`, `ZSTD_getErrorName`, `ZSTD_getErrorCode`,\n`ZSTD_getErrorString`, `ERR_getErrorString`.\nCtx: `ZSTD_createCCtx`, `ZSTD_createCCtx_advanced`, `ZSTD_freeCCtx`, `ZSTD_sizeof_CCtx`,\n`ZSTD_createDCtx`, `ZSTD_createDCtx_advanced`, `ZSTD_freeDCtx`, `ZSTD_sizeof_DCtx`,\n`ZSTD_copyCCtx`, `ZSTD_copyDCtx`.\n\n### (b) advanced one-shot\n`ZSTD_compress2`, `ZSTD_compress_advanced`, `ZSTD_compress_advanced_internal`,\n`ZSTD_compress_usingDict`, `ZSTD_compress_usingCDict`, `ZSTD_compress_usingCDict_advanced`,\n`ZSTD_decompress_usingDict`, `ZSTD_decompress_usingDDict`.\nParams objects: `ZSTD_createCCtxParams`, `ZSTD_freeCCtxParams`, `ZSTD_CCtxParams_init`,\n`ZSTD_CCtxParams_init_advanced`, `ZSTD_CCtxParams_reset`, `ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter`,\n`ZSTD_CCtxParams_getParameter`, `ZSTD_CCtx_setParametersUsingCCtxParams`,\n`ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter`, `ZSTD_CCtx_getParameter`, `ZSTD_CCtx_setCParams`,\n`ZSTD_CCtx_setFParams`, `ZSTD_CCtx_setParams`, `ZSTD_CCtx_setPledgedSrcSize`,\n`ZSTD_CCtx_reset`, `ZSTD_DCtx_setParameter`, `ZSTD_DCtx_getParameter`, `ZSTD_DCtx_reset`,\n`ZSTD_DCtx_setFormat`, `ZSTD_DCtx_setMaxWindowSize`, `ZSTD_cParam_getBounds`,\n`ZSTD_dParam_getBounds`, `ZSTD_getCParams`, `ZSTD_getParams`,\n`ZSTD_getCParamsFromCCtxParams`, `ZSTD_getCParamsFromCDict`, `ZSTD_checkCParams`,\n`ZSTD_adjustCParams`, `ZSTD_cycleLog`, `ZSTD_CCtx_refThreadPool`, `ZSTD_CCtx_trace`,\n`ZSTD_getFrameProgression`, `ZSTD_toFlushNow`, `ZSTD_getSeqStore`.\n\n### (c) streaming\nCompression: `ZSTD_compressStream`, `ZSTD_compressStream2`,\n`ZSTD_compressStream2_simpleArgs`, `ZSTD_flushStream`, `ZSTD_endStream`,\n`ZSTD_initCStream`, `ZSTD_initCStream_srcSize`, `ZSTD_initCStream_advanced`,\n`ZSTD_initCStream_usingDict`, `ZSTD_initCStream_usingCDict`,\n`ZSTD_initCStream_usingCDict_advanced`, `ZSTD_initCStream_internal`,\n`ZSTD_resetCStream`, `ZSTD_createCStream`, `ZSTD_createCStream_advanced`,\n`ZSTD_freeCStream`, `ZSTD_sizeof_CStream`, `ZSTD_CStreamInSize`, `ZSTD_CStreamOutSize`.\nDecompression: `ZSTD_decompressStream`, `ZSTD_decompressStream_simpleArgs`,\n`ZSTD_initDStream`, `ZSTD_initDStream_usingDict`, `ZSTD_initDStream_usingDDict`,\n`ZSTD_resetDStream`, `ZSTD_createDStream`, `ZSTD_createDStream_advanced`,\n`ZSTD_freeDStream`, `ZSTD_sizeof_DStream`, `ZSTD_DStreamInSize`, `ZSTD_DStreamOutSize`,\n`ZSTD_decodingBufferSize_min`.\nDirectives: `ZSTD_e_continue=0`, `ZSTD_e_flush=1`, `ZSTD_e_end=2`.\nReset directives: `ZSTD_reset_session_only=1`, `ZSTD_reset_parameters=2`,\n`ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters=3`.\n\n### (d) block-level / lowest level\nCompress: `ZSTD_compressBegin`, `ZSTD_compressBegin_usingDict`,\n`ZSTD_compressBegin_advanced`, `ZSTD_compressBegin_advanced_internal`,\n`ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict`, `ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict_advanced`,\n`ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict_deprecated`, `ZSTD_compressContinue`,\n`ZSTD_compressContinue_public`, `ZSTD_compressEnd`, `ZSTD_compressEnd_public`,\n`ZSTD_compressBlock`, `ZSTD_compressBlock_deprecated`, `ZSTD_getBlockSize`.\nDecompress: `ZSTD_decompressBegin`, `ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDict`,\n`ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDDict`, `ZSTD_decompressContinue`,\n`ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompress`, `ZSTD_nextInputType`, `ZSTD_decompressBlock`,\n`ZSTD_decompressBlock_deprecated`, `ZSTD_decompressBlock_internal`, `ZSTD_insertBlock`,\n`ZSTD_getcBlockSize`, `ZSTD_decodeSeqHeaders`, `ZSTD_decodeLiteralsBlock_wrapper`,\n`ZSTD_buildFSETable`, `ZSTD_checkContinuity`.\n`ZSTD_nextInputType_e`: `ZSTDnit_frameHeader`, `ZSTDnit_blockHeader`, `ZSTDnit_block`,\n`ZSTDnit_lastBlock`, `ZSTDnit_checksum`, `ZSTDnit_skippableFrame`.\n`ZSTD_getBlockSize()` = `MIN(appliedParams.maxBlockSize, 1 << cParams.windowLog)`\n(`zstd_compress.c:4869-4880`); `ZSTD_compressBlock` errors if `srcSize >` that.\n`ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompressWithInputSize` allows a **partial** block only when\n`bType == bt_raw` in stage `ZSTDds_decompressBlock`/`ZSTDds_decompressLastBlock`.\n\n### (e) sequence-level\n`ZSTD_generateSequences`, `ZSTD_mergeBlockDelimiters`, `ZSTD_compressSequences`,\n`ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals`, `ZSTD_sequenceBound`, `ZSTD_convertBlockSequences`,\n`ZSTD_registerSequenceProducer`, `ZSTD_CCtxParams_registerSequenceProducer`,\n`ZSTD_getSeqStore`, `ZSTD_resetSeqStore`, `ZSTD_seqToCodes`.\n`ZSTD_sequenceBound(srcSize) = (srcSize/ZSTD_MINMATCH_MIN + 1) + (srcSize/ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX_MIN + 1)`\n(`zstd_compress.c:3514-3517`).\n`ZSTD_generateSequences` errors if `ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize != 0` or `ZSTD_c_nbWorkers != 0`.\n`ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals` errors unless\n`blockDelimiters == ZSTD_sf_explicitBlockDelimiters`, `validateSequences == 0`,\n`checksumFlag == 0`, and `litCapacity >= litSize` (+8 recommended).\n\n### (f) static / preallocated\n`ZSTD_initStaticCCtx`, `ZSTD_initStaticDCtx`, `ZSTD_initStaticCDict`,\n`ZSTD_initStaticDDict`, `ZSTD_initStaticCStream`, `ZSTD_initStaticDStream`.\nEstimators: `ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize`, `ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize_usingCParams`,\n`ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize_usingCCtxParams`, `ZSTD_estimateCStreamSize`,\n`ZSTD_estimateCStreamSize_usingCParams`, `ZSTD_estimateCStreamSize_usingCCtxParams`,\n`ZSTD_estimateCDictSize`, `ZSTD_estimateCDictSize_advanced`, `ZSTD_estimateDCtxSize`,\n`ZSTD_estimateDStreamSize`, `ZSTD_estimateDStreamSize_fromFrame`,\n`ZSTD_estimateDDictSize`.\n\n### (g) dictionary\nCDict: `ZSTD_create