row 0 with `targetLength = -level`, which also auto-disables literal compression. **Quirk worth its own test row**: `ZSTD_getCParamRowSize` computes `srcSizeHint + dictSize + 500` when srcSize is UNKNOWN, and since UNKNOWN is `(U64)-1` this **wraps to `dictSize + 499`** — so \"unknown size + dictionary\" picks a *small* table.\n\n**AXIS 3** — 21 stable + 20 experimental params with exact enum values (note `ZSTD_c_format = experimentalParam2 = 10`, not in the 1000-range). `ZSTD_c_prefetchCDictTables` is prefetch-only and must be byte-identical. `ZSTD_c_deterministicRefPrefix=1` is the only deterministic way to reach the `*_extDict` compressors.\n\n**AXIS 4** — all 615 exported symbols grouped (a)–(o). **Verified the legacy claim**: `zstd_legacy.h` includes v0N under `#if (ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT <= N)`, so at 5 only v05/v06/v07 auto-dispatch through `ZSTD_decompress`/`ZSTD_decompressStream`. But `file(GLOB \"src/legacy/*.c\")` compiles all seven files with no body guards, so **all v01–v07 symbols are exported and directly callable** — they're just unreachable via dispatch. Also found: `ZSTDv02/03_decompressDCtx`, `ZSTDv04_isError`, and `ZSTDv06_compressBound` are declared in headers but never defined/exported.\n\n**AXIS 5** — every boundary constant traced to source, incl. the `srcSize < 7` raw threshold (`MIN_CBLOCK_SIZE+ZSTD_blockHeaderSize+1+1`), `rleMaxLength=25` plus the `!isFirstBlock` rule (a single-block all-same-byte frame is *never* RLE), `ZSTD_minLiteralsToCompress = 8 << MIN(9-strategy, 3)`, and the fcs/dictID field-width tables.\n\n**PROPOSED CONFIG ROWS: 120** (within the requested 60–120), covering all 40 block compressors, all 4 clevel row sets, every parameter, all 15 entry-point tiers including the block-level, sequence-level, static, and legacy tiers, and every input-shape boundary.","usage":{"total_tokens":255158,"tool_uses":62,"duration_ms":1157618},"uuid":"8ab49d0d-7e0f-4836-854e-06c6a20042f9","session_id":"f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5"}
