{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a1f08216953d1c6df","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01EzvN6VL3gn3YxcTHBLJCuB","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-KufEFj-translated-rust/f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5/tasks/a1f08216953d1c6df.output","summary":"Fixed. `ldm_fast_repro` now reports `test result: ok` with zero diverging configs (was 221), and `rows_29_57_ldm_parameter_combinations` also passes.\n\n## Changes — both in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust/src/compress/zstd_ldm.rs`\n\n**1. `ZSTD_ldm_gear_reset` — spurious write-back of the rolling hash (was line 227)**\n\n```rust\n-    (*state).rolling = hash;     // REMOVED\n+    let _ = hash;\n```\n\nC ground truth (`c_src/src/compress/zstd_ldm.c:65-85`) reads `state->rolling` into a local `hash`, iterates it over `minMatchLength` bytes, and then **never stores it back**. I verified this mechanically: the only writes to `->rolling` in the whole C file are line 37 (`gear_init`) and line 131 (`gear_feed`). So in C, `ZSTD_ldm_gear_reset` is effectively a no-op on the state — the \"reset\" is dead code. The Rust translator \"helpfully\" added the store, which meant every call (the one at the top of `ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences_internal`, and the overlap-skip call in the match loop) seeded the gear hash with a completely different value than C, shifting all split points and therefore all LDM match positions. This was the dominant cause of the divergence.\n\n**2. `ZSTD_ldm_gear_init` — complement taken at the wrong width (line 175)**\n\n```rust\n-    (*state).rolling = !(0u32 as U64);   // == 0xFFFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFF\n+    (*state).rolling = (!0u32) as U64;   // == 0x0000_0000_FFFF_FFFF\n```\n\nC is `state->rolling = ~(U32)0;` — the `~` applies at `U32` width giving `0xFFFFFFFF`, which is *then* widened to the `U64` field. The Rust cast `0u32 as U64` happened *before* the `!`, producing `u64::MAX`. Since the stop-mask tests high bits of the rolling hash, the extra high bits changed split detection for roughly the first 32 bytes of every gear pass. This bug was latent/masked while bug 1 existed but had to be fixed too.\n\n## Verified-correct (no change needed)\n- All 256 `ZSTD_ldm_gearTab` entries match `zstd_ldm_geartab.h` exactly and in order (compared programmatically; the table is 256 entries, not 64).\n- `ldmEntry_t` / `ldmMatchCandidate_t` / `ldmState_t` / `ldmParams_t` field order and `#[repr(C)]` match; `LDM_BATCH_SIZE=64`, `HASH_READ_SIZE=8` match.\n- `gear_feed` chunked loop + `goto done`/`break 'done` equivalence, `wrapping_add` placement, `BOUNDED`/`MIN` semantics, bucket indexing and the `bucketOffsets` wraparound, both `countBackwardsMatch` variants, `generateSequences_internal`'s candidate/bucket loops with manual `n++`/`cur++` on every `continue` path, the chunking arithmetic in `generateSequences`, and `skipSequences`/`skipRawSeqStoreBytes`/`maybeSplitSequence`/`blockCompress` all mirror C.\n\n## Pre-existing unrelated failure\n`tests/phase_b_params.rs::rows_29_57_randomized_parameter_soup` fails at `soup iter=100 shape=LongRange len=3 params=[…(160, 2)…]`. I confirmed this is **not** caused by my change by reverting both edits, rebuilding, and reproducing the identical failure at the identical iteration. That config has LDM at `2` (auto/disabled) on a 3-byte input, so it is outside the LDM match-finder path — a separate bug elsewhere in the port.","usage":{"total_tokens":72034,"tool_uses":18,"duration_ms":386784},"uuid":"0ed5619e-9c20-4a18-9df9-c22bef2a9bf7","session_id":"f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01EzvN6VL3gn3YxcTHBLJCuB","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. `ldm_fast_repro` now reports `test result: ok` with zero diverging configs (was 221), and `rows_29_57_ldm_parameter_combinations` also passes.\n\n## Changes — both in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust/src/compress/zstd_ldm.rs`\n\n**1. `ZSTD_ldm_gear_reset` — spurious write-back of the rolling hash (was line 227)**\n\n```rust\n-    (*state).rolling = hash;     // REMOVED\n+    let _ = hash;\n```\n\nC ground truth (`c_src/src/compress/zstd_ldm.c:65-85`) reads `state->rolling` into a local `hash`, iterates it over `minMatchLength` bytes, and then **never stores it back**. I verified this mechanically: the only writes to `->rolling` in the whole C file are line 37 (`gear_init`) and line 131 (`gear_feed`). So in C, `ZSTD_ldm_gear_reset` is effectively a no-op on the state — the \"reset\" is dead code. The Rust translator \"helpfully\" added the store, which meant every call (the one at the top of `ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences_internal`, and the overlap-skip call in the match loop) seeded the gear hash with a completely different value than C, shifting all split points and therefore all LDM match positions. This was the dominant cause of the divergence.\n\n**2. `ZSTD_ldm_gear_init` — complement taken at the wrong width (line 175)**\n\n```rust\n-    (*state).rolling = !(0u32 as U64);   // == 0xFFFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFF\n+    (*state).rolling = (!0u32) as U64;   // == 0x0000_0000_FFFF_FFFF\n```\n\nC is `state->rolling = ~(U32)0;` — the `~` applies at `U32` width giving `0xFFFFFFFF`, which is *then* widened to the `U64` field. The Rust cast `0u32 as U64` happened *before* the `!`, producing `u64::MAX`. Since the stop-mask tests high bits of the rolling hash, the extra high bits changed split detection for roughly the first 32 bytes of every gear pass. This bug was latent/masked while bug 1 existed but had to be fixed too.\n\n## Verified-correct (no change needed)\n- All 256 `ZSTD_ldm_gearTab` entries match `zstd_ldm_geartab.h` exactly and in order (compared programmatically; the table is 256 entries, not 64).\n- `ldmEntry_t` / `ldmMatchCandidate_t` / `ldmState_t` / `ldmParams_t` field order and `#[repr(C)]` match; `LDM_BATCH_SIZE=64`, `HASH_READ_SIZE=8` match.\n- `gear_feed` chunked loop + `goto done`/`break 'done` equivalence, `wrapping_add` placement, `BOUNDED`/`MIN` semantics, bucket indexing and the `bucketOffsets` wraparound, both `countBackwardsMatch` variants, `generateSequences_internal`'s candidate/bucket loops with manual `n++`/`cur++` on every `continue` path, the chunking arithmetic in `generateSequences`, and `skipSequences`/`skipRawSeqStoreBytes`/`maybeSplitSequence`/`blockCompress` all mirror C.\n\n## Pre-existing unrelated failure\n`tests/phase_b_params.rs::rows_29_57_randomized_parameter_soup` fails at `soup iter=100 shape=LongRange len=3 params=[…(160, 2)…]`. I confirmed this is **not** caused by my change by reverting both edits, rebuilding, and reproducing the identical failure at the identical iteration. That config has LDM at `2` (auto/disabled) on a 3-byte input, so it is outside the LDM match-finder path — a separate bug elsewhere in the port."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a1f08216953d1c6df (use SendMessage with to: 'a1f08216953d1c6df', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 73269\ntool_uses: 18\nduration_ms: 386785</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5","uuid":"121ecf09-576a-47aa-8513-ff29e9e4a41f","timestamp":"2026-08-14T21:29:45.307Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust\n\nA C-to-Rust translation of zstd v1.5.7 has a CONFIRMED BUG in the Long Distance Matching (LDM) code. The C code is GROUND TRUTH and must NOT be modified. Fix ONLY the Rust.\n\n## Files\n- C ground truth: `c_src/src/compress/zstd_ldm.c` (~700 lines) and `c_src/src/compress/zstd_ldm.h`, plus `c_src/src/compress/zstd_ldm_geartab.h` (a table of 64 u64 constants).\n- Rust translation to FIX: `src/compress/zstd_ldm.rs` (1036 lines).\n\n## The divergence (already isolated for you)\nCompressing 132000 bytes of \"long range\" data (a repeated 4KB motif separated by\nrandom filler) with `ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching=1` produces DIFFERENT\ncompressed bytes between C and Rust. 221 out of 240 parameter combinations of\n(windowLog, ldmHashLog, ldmMinMatch, ldmBucketSizeLog, ldmHashRateLog) diverge.\nDivergence appears only when LDM is EXPLICITLY enabled (value 1); with value 0\nor 2 (auto/disable) output matches. Non-long-range data shapes all match.\nSometimes the total compressed size is identical but individual bytes differ,\nand sometimes the size differs by 1-2 bytes — so this is a match-finding\ndifference, not a framing/header difference.\n\n## Your job\nDo a careful LINE-BY-LINE comparison of `zstd_ldm.c` against `src/compress/zstd_ldm.rs`\nand find every place the Rust deviates. Pay particular attention to these\nfunctions, which are where such bugs hide:\n\n- `ZSTD_ldm_gear_init`, `ZSTD_ldm_gear_reset`, `ZSTD_ldm_gear_feed`\n  (the rolling gear hash: check the bit masking, the `XXH64`/rotation constants,\n  the `LDM_MIN_MATCH_LENGTH` handling, the `hashRateLog`/`stepSize` logic,\n  and especially the loop structure of `ZSTD_ldm_gear_feed` which processes\n  input in chunks and can emit multiple split points)\n- `ZSTD_ldm_getBucket`, `ZSTD_ldm_insertEntry` (bucket indexing, the\n  `bucketOffsets` byte counter wraparound, `1 << bucketSizeLog`)\n- `ZSTD_ldm_countBackwardsMatch`, `ZSTD_ldm_countBackwardsMatch_2segments`\n- `ZSTD_ldm_fillFastTables`, `ZSTD_ldm_fillHashTable`, `ZSTD_ldm_limitTableUpdate`\n- `ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences_internal` (the main loop: `ZSTD_count`,\n  `ZSTD_count_2segments`, the candidate selection loop over the bucket, the\n  `bestEntry`/`forwardMatchLength`/`backwardMatchLength` selection, the\n  `minMatchLength` comparison, the `curForwardMatchLength` filter, and how\n  `anchor`/`ip`/`splits` advance)\n- `ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences` (chunking by `maxChunkSize`, the\n  `ZSTD_window_update` / `loadedDictEnd` / `nbChunks` arithmetic, and the\n  `ZSTD_ldm_limitTableUpdate` call sites)\n- `ZSTD_ldm_blockCompress`, `ZSTD_ldm_skipSequences`, `ZSTD_ldm_skipRawSeqStoreBytes`\n- `ZSTD_ldm_adjustParameters`, `ZSTD_ldm_getTableSize`, `ZSTD_ldm_getMaxNbSeq`\n\nCommon translation bugs to check for specifically:\n1. Signed vs unsigned comparison, and `U32`/`U64`/`size_t` width mistakes.\n2. Missing `wrapping_*` where C relies on integer wraparound, or spurious\n   `wrapping_*` that changes a comparison.\n3. Off-by-one in loop bounds (`<` vs `<=`), and `do {} while` vs `while` semantics.\n4. Pointer arithmetic that should be on `BYTE*` but got done on a typed pointer.\n5. The gear-table constants in `zstd_ldm_geartab.h` — verify ALL 64 values are\n   transcribed correctly and in the right order.\n6. `ZSTD_highbit32` / `ZSTD_NbCommonBytes` / `ZSTD_count` helper differences.\n7. Struct field order/padding in `ldmState_t`, `ldmEntry_t`, `ldmMatchCandidate_t`,\n   `rawSeqStore_t`, `ldmParams_t` — these are shared across the ABI.\n8. `memcpy`/`memmove`/`memset` sizes computed with the wrong element size\n   (e.g. forgetting `* sizeof(ldmEntry_t)`).\n\n## How to verify your fix\nBuild the Rust cdylib and run the dedicated regression test:\n\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust\ncargo build --release 2>&1 | tail -3\ntimeout 300 cargo test --release --test repro_ldm ldm_fast_repro 2>&1 | tail -20\n```\n\nThe test `ldm_fast_repro` currently reports \"221 LDM configs diverge\". It must\nreport `test result: ok` with ZERO diverging configs. The test loads BOTH the C\n`.so` and the Rust `.so` via libloading and compares compressed bytes.\n\nIterate until that test passes. Do NOT modify:\n- anything under `c_src/`\n- `tests/` (the test is correct; the Rust library is wrong)\n- `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`\n\nReport exactly which lines you changed and why each was wrong.","agentId":"a1f08216953d1c6df","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. `ldm_fast_repro` now reports `test result: ok` with zero diverging configs (was 221), and `rows_29_57_ldm_parameter_combinations` also passes.\n\n## Changes — both in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust/src/compress/zstd_ldm.rs`\n\n**1. `ZSTD_ldm_gear_reset` — spurious write-back of the rolling hash (was line 227)**\n\n```rust\n-    (*state).rolling = hash;     // REMOVED\n+    let _ = hash;\n```\n\nC ground truth (`c_src/src/compress/zstd_ldm.c:65-85`) reads `state->rolling` into a local `hash`, iterates it over `minMatchLength` bytes, and then **never stores it back**. I verified this mechanically: the only writes to `->rolling` in the whole C file are line 37 (`gear_init`) and line 131 (`gear_feed`). So in C, `ZSTD_ldm_gear_reset` is effectively a no-op on the state — the \"reset\" is dead code. The Rust translator \"helpfully\" added the store, which meant every call (the one at the top of `ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences_internal`, and the overlap-skip call in the match loop) seeded the gear hash with a completely different value than C, shifting all split points and therefore all LDM match positions. This was the dominant cause of the divergence.\n\n**2. `ZSTD_ldm_gear_init` — complement taken at the wrong width (line 175)**\n\n```rust\n-    (*state).rolling = !(0u32 as U64);   // == 0xFFFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFF\n+    (*state).rolling = (!0u32) as U64;   // == 0x0000_0000_FFFF_FFFF\n```\n\nC is `state->rolling = ~(U32)0;` — the `~` applies at `U32` width giving `0xFFFFFFFF`, which is *then* widened to the `U64` field. The Rust cast `0u32 as U64` happened *before* the `!`, producing `u64::MAX`. Since the stop-mask tests high bits of the rolling hash, the extra high bits changed split detection for roughly the first 32 bytes of every gear pass. This bug was latent/masked while bug 1 existed but had to be fixed too.\n\n## Verified-correct (no change needed)\n- All 256 `ZSTD_ldm_gearTab` entries match `zstd_ldm_geartab.h` exactly and in order (compared programmatically; the table is 256 entries, not 64).\n- `ldmEntry_t` / `ldmMatchCandidate_t` / `ldmState_t` / `ldmParams_t` field order and `#[repr(C)]` match; `LDM_BATCH_SIZE=64`, `HASH_READ_SIZE=8` match.\n- `gear_feed` chunked loop + `goto done`/`break 'done` equivalence, `wrapping_add` placement, `BOUNDED`/`MIN` semantics, bucket indexing and the `bucketOffsets` wraparound, both `countBackwardsMatch` variants, `generateSequences_internal`'s candidate/bucket loops with manual `n++`/`cur++` on every `continue` path, the chunking arithmetic in `generateSequences`, and `skipSequences`/`skipRawSeqStoreBytes`/`maybeSplitSequence`/`blockCompress` all mirror C.\n\n## Pre-existing unrelated failure\n`tests/phase_b_params.rs::rows_29_57_randomized_parameter_soup` fails at `soup iter=100 shape=LongRange len=3 params=[…(160, 2)…]`. I confirmed this is **not** caused by my change by reverting both edits, rebuilding, and reproducing the identical failure at the identical iteration. That config has LDM at `2` (auto/disabled) on a 3-byte input, so it is outside the LDM match-finder path — a separate bug elsewhere in the port."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":386785,"totalTokens":73269,"totalToolUseCount":18,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":562,"cache_read_input_tokens":71276,"output_tokens":1429,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":62},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":562},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":2,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":14,"editFileCount":2,"linesAdded":11,"linesRemoved":6,"otherToolCount":0}}}
