{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01FwyHY6a3Ut6ME6WRCrGdtX","type":"tool_result","content":"# CONFIGS.md — CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE (Phase A artifact)\n\nThe mirror of `ERRORS.md`: the enumeration of **VALID** input configurations that\nthe C code treats DIFFERENTLY. Derived from the branches the C source actually\ntakes (`if` / `switch` / dispatch tables), not from documentation.\n\n## Build configuration (from `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` — the only one built)\n\n```\nZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5   XXH_NAMESPACE=ZSTD_   DYNAMIC_BMI2=0\nZSTD_MULTITHREAD NOT defined   -> nbWorkers/jobSize/overlapLog bounds are [0,0]\nno ZSTD_EXCLUDE_*_BLOCK_COMPRESSOR -> the full 40-symbol dispatch matrix is live\n```\n\n`file(GLOB src/legacy/*.c)` compiles ALL of v01..v07, so every `ZSTDv0N_*` /\n`ZBUFFv0N_*` symbol is exported and directly callable. But `zstd_legacy.h` guards\ndispatch with `#if (ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT <= N)`, so only **v05, v06, v07** frames\nauto-dispatch through `ZSTD_decompress` / `ZSTD_decompressStream`. v01..v04 are\nreachable only by calling their symbols directly.\n\n## Cargo features\n\n`translated_rust/Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]` section**, so there is\nexactly ONE build configuration: the default (empty feature set). Phase D's\n\"repeat for every feature combination\" therefore reduces to this single combo,\nwhich is verified explicitly in `tests/feature_matrix.rs`.\n\n## Checkbox column\n\n`[x]` = row passes byte-identical C-vs-Rust differential testing across\nrandomized inputs (fixed seed) via the `.so` exports of BOTH libraries.\n\n\nShorthand: `L<n>` = `ZSTD_c_compressionLevel=n`; `S=x` = `ZSTD_c_strategy=x`;\n`row=E/D/A` = `ZSTD_c_useRowMatchFinder = enable/disable/auto`;\n`detRP` = `ZSTD_c_deterministicRefPrefix=1`; `pSS` = pledgedSrcSize;\n`attach` = CDict + `ZSTD_c_forceAttachDict=ZSTD_dictForceAttach`;\n`DDS` = CDict built by `ZSTD_createCDict_advanced2` with `ZSTD_c_enableDedicatedDictSearch=1`.\n\"200K text\" = 200 KB compressible text; \"rand N\" = N incompressible bytes;\n\"rle N\" = N identical bytes. D32 = 32 KB trained zstd dictionary.\nRows marked with a sub-case list are one configuration *family*; expand each listed value.\n\n### Part 1 — AXIS 1 block-compressor dispatch (covers all 40 reachable symbols), rows 1-12\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|1| `ZSTD_compress2`; +`ZSTD_CCtx_refPrefix`; +`ZSTD_CCtx_refCDict` | `S=ZSTD_fast`, 200K text, dictMode sub-cases: noDict -> `ZSTD_compressBlock_fast`; refPrefix+`detRP` -> `_fast_extDict`; `attach`(D32) -> `_fast_dictMatchState`  [ ] |\n|2| same three | `S=ZSTD_dfast`, 200K text -> `_doubleFast` / `_doubleFast_extDict` / `_doubleFast_dictMatchState`  [ ] |\n|3| same three | `S=ZSTD_btlazy2`, 200K text -> `_btlazy2` / `_btlazy2_extDict` / `_btlazy2_dictMatchState`  [ ] |\n|4| same three | `S=ZSTD_btopt`, `splitAfterSequences=disable`, 200K text -> `_btopt` / `_btopt_extDict` / `_btopt_dictMatchState`  [ ] |\n|5| same three | `S=ZSTD_btultra`, 200K text -> `_btultra` / `_btultra_extDict` / `_btultra_dictMatchState`  [ ] |\n|6| same three | `S=ZSTD_btultra2`, 200K text -> `_btultra2` / **alias** `_btultra_extDict` / **alias** `_btultra_dictMatchState` (verify the btultra2->btultra aliasing)  [ ] |\n|7| `ZSTD_compress2`; +refPrefix; +refCDict; +DDS CDict | `S=ZSTD_greedy`, `row=D`, 200K text; 4 dictMode sub-cases -> `_greedy` / `_greedy_extDict` / `_greedy_dictMatchState` / `_greedy_dedicatedDictSearch`  [ ] |\n|8| same four | `S=ZSTD_greedy`, `row=E` -> `_greedy_row` / `_greedy_extDict_row` / `_greedy_dictMatchState_row` / `_greedy_dedicatedDictSearch_row`  [ ] |\n|9| same four | `S=ZSTD_lazy`, `row=D` -> `_lazy` / `_lazy_extDict` / `_lazy_dictMatchState` / `_lazy_dedicatedDictSearch`  [ ] |\n|10| same four | `S=ZSTD_lazy`, `row=E` -> `_lazy_row` / `_lazy_extDict_row` / `_lazy_dictMatchState_row` / `_lazy_dedicatedDictSearch_row`  [ ] |\n|11| same four | `S=ZSTD_lazy2`, `row=D` -> `_lazy2` / `_lazy2_extDict` / `_lazy2_dictMatchState` / `_lazy2_dedicatedDictSearch`  [ ] |\n|12| same four | `S=ZSTD_lazy2`, `row=E` -> `_lazy2_row` / `_lazy2_extDict_row` / `_lazy2_dictMatchState_row` / `_lazy2_dedicatedDictSearch_row`  [ ] |\n\n### Part 2 — row-match-finder resolution, rows 13-16\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|13| `ZSTD_compress` | `L=5` (greedy) on 8K text -> tableID 3, `windowLog=14`, auto -> row **OFF** (`_greedy`); vs `L=5` on 200K text -> `windowLog=21`, auto -> row **ON** (`_greedy_row`)  [ ] |\n|14| `ZSTD_compress2` | `S=ZSTD_lazy2`, `row=A`, explicit `windowLog` = 14 (OFF) vs 15 (ON) — the `> 14` boundary  [ ] |\n|15| `ZSTD_compress2` | `S=ZSTD_lazy2`, `row=E`, `searchLog` = 4 / 5 / 6 -> `rowLog = BOUNDED(4,searchLog,6)` = 16- / 32- / 64-entry rows  [ ] |\n|16| `ZSTD_compress2` + refCDict | CCtx `row=E` but CDict built with `row=D` (and vice versa) — the CDict's `useRowMatchFinder` must override on attach  [ ] |\n\n### Part 3 — AXIS 2 levels and cParam derivation, rows 17-28\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|17| `ZSTD_compress` | `L=0` -> row 3 (default), 200K text  [ ] |\n|18| `ZSTD_compress` | `L=1` (row 1, `targetLength=0`, literals compressed), 200K text  [ ] |\n|19| `ZSTD_compress` | `L=-1` -> row 0 + `targetLength=1`; literal compression auto-**disabled**; 200K text  [ ] |\n|20| `ZSTD_compress` | negative sweep: `L` = -5 / -1000 / -131072 (`ZSTD_minCLevel`) / -200000 (clamps to -131072), 200K text  [ ] |\n|21| `ZSTD_compress` | `L=22` (`ZSTD_maxCLevel`) and `L=99` (clamps to 22), 200K text  [ ] |\n|22| `ZSTD_compress` | `L=3` at each tableID boundary: srcSize = 16384 / 16385 / 131072 / 131073 / 262144 / 262145  [ ] |\n|23| `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_srcSizeHint` | streaming (real size unknown), `srcSizeHint` = 0 / 16384 / 16385 / 131073 / 262145 / INT_MAX — forces each tableID  [ ] |\n