bled zstd won't allocate an input window buffer,\n2153- * because the user guarantees it can reference the ZSTD_inBuffer until\n2154- * the frame is complete. But, it will still allocate an output buffer\n2155: * large enough to fit a block (see ZSTD_c_stableOutBuffer). This will also\n2156- * avoid the memcpy() from the input buffer to the input window buffer.\n2157- *\n2158- * NOTE: So long as the ZSTD_inBuffer always points to valid memory, using\n2159- * this flag is ALWAYS memory safe, and will never access out-of-bounds\n2160- * memory. However, compression WILL fail if conditions are not respected.\n2161- *","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01YNXnHPsGBqwCpksc3jfqzQ","session_id":"f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5","uuid":"d1fdc9cc-06a2-4ec4-b176-25a1d6adde27","timestamp":"2026-08-14T21:34:21.475Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write streaming and block-level tests"}
