{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xssxzc3izg6ftphbb4363t3pwvovkklvnboxvkqjznred5c472ba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_011YDfa5uGtCzKrgciqkC7an","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write legacy and zbuff tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust\n\nYou are writing a DIFFERENTIAL TEST file for a C-to-Rust translation of zstd 1.5.7.\nThe C code is GROUND TRUTH. The Rust must match byte-for-byte.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n1. Create EXACTLY ONE new file: `tests/phase_b_legacy_zbuff.rs`. Do not modify any other file.\n   NEVER modify `c_src/`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`,\n   or other test files.\n2. If a test reveals C and Rust DIFFER, that is a REAL BUG in the Rust library.\n   DO NOT weaken, skip, `#[ignore]`, or loosen the assertion. LEAVE the strict\n   assertion and REPORT the divergence with the exact failing configuration.\n3. Never call Rust functions directly — always through the loaded `.so`.\n\n## Existing harness (`mod common; use common::*;`)\nProvides `capi()`, `rapi()` (`&'static Api`), `pair::<FnType>(\"Sym\")`,\n`sym::<FnType>(c_lib()|r_lib(),\"Sym\")`, `both_have(\"Sym\")`, `is_error`, `err_code`,\n`err_name(lib,code)`, `assert_bytes_eq`, `assert_ret_eq`, `diff(ctx,|api|->T)`,\n`Out{ret,bytes}`/`Out::ok`/`Out::err`/`diff_out`, `Rng::new(seed)` with\n`.next_u64/.next_u32/.below/.range/.byte`, `Shape::{Rle,Random,Text,Skewed,LongRange,Records}`,\n`ALL_SHAPES`, `gen(shape,len,&mut rng)`, `gen_samples(...)`, plus `ZSTD_inBuffer`,\n`ZSTD_outBuffer`, `ZSTD_customMem`, and the `ZSTD_c_*`/`ZSTD_d_*` constants.\n`Api` includes `createCCtx/freeCCtx/createDCtx/freeDCtx/compress2/compress/\ncompressBound/decompress/decompressDCtx/setParameter/loadDictionary/...`.\n\n## Build context you MUST know\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` defines `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5` and globs ALL of\n`src/legacy/*.c`. Consequences:\n- ALL of v01..v07's symbols are compiled and EXPORTED, so every `ZSTDv0N_*` and\n  `ZBUFFv0N_*` symbol is directly callable via dlsym in BOTH libraries.\n- BUT `c_src/src/legacy/zstd_legacy.h` guards dispatch with\n  `#if (ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT <= N)`, so only **v05, v06, v07** frames are\n  auto-dispatched by the modern `ZSTD_decompress` / `ZSTD_decompressStream`.\nVerify this behaviour differentially rather than assuming it.\n\n## What to test — CONFIGS.md rows covering the deprecated + legacy tiers\n\n### 1. Deprecated ZBUFF_* tier (header: `c_src/src/deprecated/zbuff.h` — READ IT)\nSymbols: `ZBUFF_createCCtx`, `ZBUFF_createCCtx_advanced`, `ZBUFF_freeCCtx`,\n`ZBUFF_compressInit`, `ZBUFF_compressInitDictionary`, `ZBUFF_compressInit_advanced`,\n`ZBUFF_compressContinue`, `ZBUFF_compressFlush`, `ZBUFF_compressEnd`,\n`ZBUFF_createDCtx`, `ZBUFF_createDCtx_advanced`, `ZBUFF_freeDCtx`,\n`ZBUFF_decompressInit`, `ZBUFF_decompressInitDictionary`, `ZBUFF_decompressContinue`,\n`ZBUFF_recommendedCInSize`, `ZBUFF_recommendedCOutSize`, `ZBUFF_recommendedDInSize`,\n`ZBUFF_recommendedDOutSize`, `ZBUFF_isError`, `ZBUFF_getErrorName`.\nThese use the older `(dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr, src, size_t* srcSizePtr)`\nin/out-pointer convention — get it EXACTLY right from the header.\nWrite a full compress round trip driving `ZBUFF_compressContinue`/`Flush`/`End`\nwith varied buffer sizes, then decompress with `ZBUFF_decompressContinue`.\nAssert identical returns, identical *dstCapacityPtr / *srcSizePtr writebacks\nafter EVERY call, and identical bytes. Cover levels 1/3/9/19, with and without a\ndictionary, and srcSize 0. Also compare all four `recommended*Size` values and\n`ZBUFF_getErrorName` over the error-code range.\n\n### 2. Legacy decoders v01..v07 — direct calls\nFor EACH version N in 01..07, the headers are `c_src/src/legacy/zstd_vNN.h`.\nREAD each header for exact signatures. Test at minimum, per version:\n- `ZSTDv0N_isError`, `ZSTDv0N_getErrorName` (where exported — v01/v02/v03/v04 may\n  not export getErrorName; use `both_have()` to gate)\n- `ZSTDv0N_decompress(dst,maxOriginalSize,src,compressedSize)`\n- `ZSTDv0N_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy(...)` — note its out-params\n- `ZSTDv0N_createDCtx` / `freeDCtx` / `resetDCtx` / `nextSrcSizeToDecompress` /\n  `decompressContinue` streaming loop\n- v05/v06/v07 extras: `ZSTDv0N_getFrameParams`, `decompressBegin`,\n  `decompressBegin_usingDict`, `decompressBlock`, `decompress_usingDict`,\n  `decompress_usingPreparedDCtx`, `copyDCtx`, `sizeofDCtx`, `ZSTDv07_createDDict`/\n  `freeDDict`/`decompress_usingDDict`/`estimateDCtxSize`/`getDecompressedSize`/\n  `isSkipFrame`/`insertBlock`\n- `ZBUFFv0N_*` streaming decoders (v04..v07): `createDCtx`, `freeDCtx`,\n  `decompressInit`, `decompressInitDictionary`, `decompressContinue`,\n  `recommendedDInSize`, `recommendedDOutSize`, `getErrorName`, `isError`.\n  v04 additionally has `ZBUFFv04_decompressWithDictionary`.\n- Also the internal-but-exported `FSEv0N_*` and `HUFv0N_*` symbols for N in\n  05/06/07 (e.g. `FSEv05_decompress`, `HUFv05_decompress`, `FSEv06_readNCount`,\n  `HUFv07_readStats`, ...). Get signatures from the corresponding `zstd_vNN.c`\n  or header. Test the simple/pure ones (`isError`, `getErrorName`,\n  `createDTable`/`freeDTable`, `decompress`) at minimum.\n\n**IMPORTANT — you do NOT have real legacy-format frames.** So:\n(a) The primary, always-valid differential check is: feed the SAME bytes to the C\n    and Rust versions of each legacy function and assert IDENTICAL return codes\n    and IDENTICAL output bytes. Use: random bytes, zeros, modern zstd frames,\n    truncated buffers, empty buffers, and hand-built buffers that begin with each\n    legacy magic number. Legacy magics: v01=0xFD2FB51E, v02=0xFD2FB522,\n    v03=0xFD2FB523, v04=0xFD2FB524, v05=0xFD2FB525, v06=0xFD2FB526,\n    v07=0xFD2FB527 (VERIFY each from the corresponding `zstd_vNN.h`/`.c`).\n    Most inputs will produce errors — that is fine and still a meaningful\n    differential test, as long as BOTH libs return the SAME error code.\n(b) Additionally fuzz: for each version, ~200 randomized buffers (with the right\n    magic prefix and random tails, plus random lengths) and assert identical\n    (return code, output bytes) from C and Rust. Use a fixed seed.\n\n### 3. Legacy auto-dispatch through the modern API\nConfirm differentially that `ZSTD_decompress`, `ZSTD_decompressStream`,\n`ZSTD_getFrameContentSize`, `ZSTD_findFrameCompressedSize` and `ZSTD_isFrame`\nbehave IDENTICALLY between C and Rust when handed buffers starting with each of\nthe seven legacy magic numbers (v01-v04 should be rejected given\nZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5; v05-v07 should enter the legacy path). Do not assert which\none happens — assert only that C and Rust AGREE.\n\n## Verify before reporting\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust\ncargo build --release 2>&1 | tail -3\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_b_legacy_zbuff 2>&1 | tail -50\n```\nThe file MUST COMPILE — iterate, checking real signatures in the C headers.\nGuard every symbol you are unsure about with `both_have(\"Name\")` so a missing\nsymbol skips rather than panics at load time. Then run and REPORT:\n- how many tests you wrote and which pass\n- for each FAILING test, the exact input and the C vs Rust values\n\nA failing test that reveals a genuine divergence is a SUCCESS. Report it."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1053,"cache_read_input_tokens":174632,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1053,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5","uuid":"aab80f15-673e-463a-8888-85035f3698d9","timestamp":"2026-08-14T21:34:36.061Z"}
