{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a8144d342920d4775","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_011YDfa5uGtCzKrgciqkC7an","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-KufEFj-translated-rust/f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5/tasks/a8144d342920d4775.output","summary":"Done. Created exactly one new file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust/tests/phase_b_legacy_zbuff.rs` (2465 lines, 22 tests). No other file was touched.\n\n## Result: 21 pass, 1 FAILS on a genuine divergence\n\n### The divergence\n\n**`HUFv07_selectDecoder(dstSize, cSrcSize)` — Rust aborts the process where C returns a value.**\n\n`c_src/src/legacy/zstd_v07.c:2449` indexes `static const algo_time_t algoTime[16][3]` with `Q = cSrcSize*16/dstSize`. The comment asserts `Q < 16` \"since dstSize > cSrcSize\", and every in-library caller (`HUFv07_decompress`, `decompress4X_DCtx`, `decompress1X_DCtx`, `decompress4X_hufOnly`) guards `cSrcSize >= dstSize` first. But `HUFv07_selectDecoder` is an **exported symbol** in both `.so`s, so an external caller can reach `Q >= 16`:\n\n| input (dstSize, cSrcSize) | Q | C result | Rust result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| (1, 1) | 16 | `0` | **panic → SIGABRT** |\n| (2, 2) | 16 | `0` | panic |\n| (256, 256) | 16 | `0` | panic |\n| (1000, 1000) | 16 | `1` | panic |\n| (4096, 4096) | 16 | `1` | panic |\n| (65536, 65536) | 16 | `1` | panic |\n| (100, 1000) | 160 | `0` | panic |\n\nRust: `panicked at src/legacy/zstd_v07.rs:2187: index out of bounds: the len is 16 but the index is 16`. Because the cdylib is built with `panic = \"abort\"`, this **kills the calling process**, whereas C reads past the static table and returns normally. (The C read is itself out-of-bounds/UB, but it does not trap and returns stable values as tabulated.)\n\nI split this into two tests so the abort is contained and attributable rather than destroying the whole binary:\n- `huf07_select_decoder_in_contract_matches` — the documented domain (`cSrcSize < dstSize`): **passes**, C == Rust for all 49 probes.\n- `huf07_select_decoder_out_of_contract_matches` — runs the raw calls in a **child process** and strictly asserts the child completes and both libs agree: **FAILS** (child exits 134/SIGABRT). No `#[ignore]`, no `should_panic`, no loosened assertion.\n\n### What the 21 passing tests cover\n\n- **ZBUFF_\\* deprecated tier** (7 tests): all 4 `recommended*Size` + cross-check vs modern equivalents; `isError`/`getErrorName` over 139 codes; full compress round trip driving `compressContinue`/`Flush`/`End` asserting return **and both `*dstCapacityPtr`/`*srcSizePtr` write-backs after every call** — levels 1/3/9/19 × srcSize {0,1,100,5000,70000} × dict/no-dict × 5 chunkings including `(1,1)` bytewise, with mid-stream flush; end-then-flush finalization per zbuff.h's literal advice; `compressInit_advanced` incl. 3 invalid-cParams cases; `createCCtx_advanced`/`createDCtx_advanced` with a custom allocator; decompress over the whole malformed corpus. The C round trip is additionally asserted to reproduce the source, validating the driver.\n- **Legacy v01..v07 direct calls** (11 tests): ~170-entry fixed corpus (all 7 legacy magics — verified BE for v01, LE for v02–v07 — × 9 tail lengths × zeros/random, truncated magics, real modern frames, dict/skippable magics) fed to `decompress`, `decompressDCtx`, `findFrameSizeInfoLegacy` (both out-params), the `createDCtx`/`resetDCtx`|`decompressBegin`/`nextSrcSizeToDecompress`/`decompressContinue` streaming loop, `getFrameParams` (v05/06/07 structs, full field compare), `decompressBegin_usingDict`+`decompressBlock`, `decompress_usingDict`, `decompress_usingPreparedDCtx`+`copyDCtx`, `sizeofDCtx`, v07 `createDDict`/`freeDDict`/`decompress_usingDDict`/`estimateDCtxSize`/`getDecompressedSize`/`isSkipFrame`/`insertBlock`/`createDCtx_advanced`, `ZBUFFv04..07_*` streaming (incl. v04's `decompressWithDictionary`), and `FSEv05/06/07_*` + `HUFv05/06/07_*` (createDTable/freeDTable, buildDTable/_raw/_rle with **full DTable image comparison**, readNCount with counter/maxSV/tableLog write-backs, decompress, decompress_usingDTable, readDTableX2/X4 with full table image, `HUFv07_readStats`, `HUFv07_decompress{1X,4X}_DCtx`).\n- **Fuzz**: 200 randomized magic-prefixed buffers per version (fixed seed), 1400 cases × `decompress` + `findFrameSizeInfoLegacy`.\n- **Auto-dispatch through the modern API**: `ZSTD_isFrame`, `getFrameContentSize`, `findFrameCompressedSize`, `isSkippableFrame`, `decompressBound`, `findDecompressedSize`, `ZSTD_decompress` (3 capacities) and `ZSTD_decompressStream` (2 chunkings, per-step `in.pos`/`out.pos`) over all 7 legacy magics. C and Rust agree everywhere — v01–v04 are rejected and v05–v07 enter the legacy path identically, matching `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5`.\n\nAlso verified up front: both `.so`s export **exactly the same 227** `ZBUFF*`/`ZSTDv*`/`FSEv*`/`HUFv*` symbols (no C-only or Rust-only). Runtime: 2.2 s.","usage":{"total_tokens":189875,"tool_uses":43,"duration_ms":934626},"uuid":"ddbc7a33-1cca-4385-bf5f-a47c5629b95a","session_id":"f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5"}
