nd explicit `blockSize+1` rejection.\n- dictID field widths driven by training a real dictionary and patching its 4-byte dictID header field, so frames genuinely carry 0/1/2/4-byte dictID fields.\n\nOne deliberate trade-off: in test 1's exhaustive small-source sweep I rotate the six input shapes by parity (`si % 2 != n % 2`) rather than running all 4×6×6×5 combinations, and I keep 1–7 byte output buffers away from >20 KB sources to avoid trace-step blowup. Both are documented in comments; every buffer size and chunk size listed in the brief is still covered."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a3f416112ac9cb696 (use SendMessage with to: 'a3f416112ac9cb696', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 215857\ntool_uses: 65\nduration_ms: 1459474</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5","uuid":"ba06efe8-f5a2-431c-8718-a3405b1f8a7b","timestamp":"2026-08-14T21:57:34.482Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust\n\nYou are writing a DIFFERENTIAL TEST file for a C-to-Rust translation of zstd 1.5.7.\nThe C code is GROUND TRUTH. The Rust must match byte-for-byte.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n1. Create EXACTLY ONE new file: `tests/phase_b_streaming.rs`. Do not modify any other file.\n   NEVER modify `c_src/`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`,\n   or other test files.\n2. If a test reveals C and Rust DIFFER, that is a REAL BUG in the Rust library.\n   DO NOT weaken, skip, `#[ignore]`, or loosen the assertion to make it pass.\n   DO NOT \"fix\" the test to accommodate the Rust behavior.\n   Instead, LEAVE the strict assertion in place and REPORT the divergence in your\n   final message with the exact failing configuration. The coordinator will fix\n   the Rust library.\n3. Never call Rust functions directly — always through the loaded `.so`.\n\n## Existing harness (already written, just `mod common; use common::*;`)\n`tests/common/mod.rs` provides:\n- `capi() -> &'static Api` and `rapi() -> &'static Api` — bundles of resolved symbols\n  for the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` respectively. Call `(api.fnName)(args)` inside `unsafe`.\n- `pair::<FnType>(\"SymbolName\") -> (c_fn, rust_fn)` for symbols not in `Api`.\n- `sym::<FnType>(c_lib(), \"Name\")` / `sym(r_lib(), ...)` for one-sided lookup.\n- `both_have(\"Name\") -> bool`.\n- Types: `ZSTD_inBuffer{src,size,pos}`, `ZSTD_outBuffer{dst,size,pos}`, `ZSTD_bounds`,\n  `ZSTD_FrameHeader{frameContentSize,windowSize,blockSizeMax,frameType,headerSize,dictID,checksumFlag,_reserved1,_reserved2}`,\n  `ZSTD_compressionParameters`, `ZSTD_frameParameters`, `ZSTD_parameters`,\n  `ZSTD_Sequence{offset,litLength,matchLength,rep}`, `ZSTD_frameProgression`, `ZSTD_customMem`.\n- Constants: `ZSTD_c_*` / `ZSTD_d_*` param ids (e.g. `ZSTD_c_checksumFlag`, `ZSTD_c_format`,\n  `ZSTD_c_stableInBuffer`, `ZSTD_c_stableOutBuffer`, `ZSTD_d_format`, `ZSTD_d_stableOutBuffer`),\n  `ALL_CPARAMS`, `ALL_DPARAMS`, `ALL_STRATEGIES`, `ZSTD_e_continue/flush/end`,\n  `ZSTD_reset_session_only/parameters/session_and_parameters`,\n  `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN`, `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_ERROR`, `ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX`,\n  `ZSTD_MAGICNUMBER`, `ZSTD_MAGIC_SKIPPABLE_START`.\n- Helpers: `is_error(usize)->bool`, `err_code(usize)->i64`, `err_name(lib,code)->String`,\n  `assert_bytes_eq(ctx,&[u8],&[u8])`, `assert_ret_eq(ctx,usize,usize)`,\n  `diff(ctx, |api| -> T)` (runs closure on both apis, requires equal `T: PartialEq+Debug`),\n  `Out{ret,bytes}` + `Out::ok(ret,&buf)` / `Out::err(ret)`, `diff_out(ctx, |api| Out)`.\n- Data gen: `Rng::new(seed)` with `.next_u64() .next_u32() .below(n) .range(lo,hi) .byte()`;\n  `Shape::{Rle,Random,Text,Skewed,LongRange,Records}`, `ALL_SHAPES`,\n  `gen(shape,len,&mut rng) -> Vec<u8>`, `gen_samples(shape,nb,min,max,&mut rng) -> (Vec<u8>,Vec<usize>)`.\n- `Api` fields you will need (all `unsafe extern \"C\"`):\n  `createCCtx() -> *mut ZSTD_CCtx`, `freeCCtx`, `createDCtx`, `freeDCtx`,\n  `compress2(cctx,dst,dstCap,src,srcSize)`, `compressBound(usize)`,\n  `decompressDCtx(dctx,dst,dstCap,src,srcSize)`,\n  `setParameter(cctx,i32,i32)`, `getParameter(cctx,i32,*mut i32)`,\n  `setPledgedSrcSize(cctx,u64)`, `cctxReset(cctx,u32)`, `dctxReset(dctx,u32)`,\n  `dSetParameter(dctx,i32,i32)`, `dGetParameter(dctx,i32,*mut i32)`,\n  `loadDictionary(cctx,ptr,len)`, `refPrefix`, `refCDict(cctx,*const ZSTD_CDict)`,\n  `createCDict(ptr,len,i32)`, `freeCDict`, `dLoadDictionary`, `dRefPrefix`,\n  `dRefDDict`, `createDDict(ptr,len)`, `freeDDict`,\n  `compressStream2(cctx,*mut ZSTD_outBuffer,*mut ZSTD_inBuffer,u32)`,\n  `compressStream(cctx,out,in)`, `flushStream(cctx,out)`, `endStream(cctx,out)`,\n  `initCStream(cctx,i32)`, `decompressStream(dctx,out,in)`, `initDStream(dctx)`,\n  `compressBegin(cctx,i32)`, `compressContinue(cctx,dst,cap,src,n)`, `compressEnd(...)`,\n  `getBlockSize(cctx)`, `compressBlock(cctx,dst,cap,src,n)`,\n  `decompressBegin(dctx)`, `decompressContinue(dctx,dst,cap,src,n)`,\n  `nextSrcSizeToDecompress(dctx)`, `nextInputType(dctx)->u32`,\n  `decompressBlock(dctx,dst,cap,src,n)`, `insertBlock(dctx,ptr,len)`,\n  `getFrameContentSize(ptr,len)->u64`, `findDecompressedSize`, `decompressBound`,\n  `findFrameCompressedSize(ptr,len)->usize`, `frameHeaderSize`,\n  `getFrameHeader(*mut ZSTD_FrameHeader,ptr,len)`, `getFrameHeaderAdvanced(...,u32)`,\n  `isFrame(ptr,len)->u32`, `isSkippableFrame(ptr,len)->u32`,\n  `getDictIDFromDict`, `getDictIDFromFrame`, `decompressionMargin`,\n  `getCParams(i32,u64,usize)`, `getParams`, `checkCParams`, `adjustCParams`, `cycleLog(u32,i32)`,\n  `sizeofCCtx(*const)`, `sizeofDCtx(*const)`.\n\n## What to test — CONFIGS.md rows 58-86 (streaming, block-level, frame utilities)\n\nWrite these `#[test]` functions. Use a FIXED SEED and MANY randomized inputs per\nscenario (at least 20-50 iterations where practical). Compare BOTH the return\ncodes AND all produced bytes AND the mutated `pos` fields of in/out buffers.\n\n### 1. `streaming_compressStream2_all_endops_and_buffer_sizes`\nDrive `ZSTD_compressStream2` in a loop with *varying* output-buffer sizes\n(1, 2, 7, 100, 1024, ZSTD_CStreamOutSize()) and varying input chunk sizes\n(1, 3, 100, 4096, all-at-once), with endOp `ZSTD_e_continue` then `ZSTD_e_flush`\nthen `ZSTD_e_end`. Assert C and Rust produce identical byte streams, identical\nper-call return values (the \"remaining to flush\" hint), and identical\n`input.pos`/`output.pos` after EVERY call. Test with levels 1, 3, 9, 19,\n`checksumFlag` 0/1, `contentSizeFlag` 0/1, pledgedSrcSize set and unset.\nInclude srcSize 0 (empty frame).\n\n### 2. `streaming_deprecated_compressStream_flush_end`\nSame but through the older `ZSTD_initCStream` + `ZSTD_compressStream` +\n`ZSTD_flushStream` + `ZSTD_endStream` tier. Also exercise\n`ZSTD_initCStream_srcSize`, `ZSTD_initCStream_usingDict`,\n`ZSTD_initCStream_advanced`, `ZSTD_initCStream_usingCDict`, `ZSTD_resetCStream`\nvia `pair::<...>()` (look up their real signatures in `c_src/src/include/zstd.h`).\n\n### 3. `streaming_decompressStream_all_buffer_sizes`\nDecompress frames (produced by the C lib) through `ZSTD_decompressStream` with\ntiny/odd output and input buffer sizes (1,2,3,7,100,1024, DStreamOutSize) so the\ndecoder must suspend and resume many times. Assert identical returns (the\n\"next input size hint\"), identical pos updates, identical output bytes. Cover\nframes with/without checksum, with/without content size, single- and multi-block,\nand multi-frame concatenations.\n\n### 4. `streaming_with_dictionary`\nStreaming compress+decompress with `loadDictionary`, `refPrefix`, `refCDict` /\n`dRefDDict`. Assert byte-identical.\n\n### 5. `streaming_stable_buffers`\nSet `ZSTD_c_stableInBuffer` and `ZSTD_c_stableOutBuffer` (1006/1007) and\n`ZSTD_d_stableOutBuffer` (1001) and drive the streaming API the way those modes\nrequire (buffer must not move). Assert identical returns and bytes, including\nthe error cases where the buffer is changed between calls.\n\n### 6. `blocklevel_compressBegin_continue_end`\nLowest-level tier: `ZSTD_compressBegin(cctx, level)` then repeated\n`ZSTD_compressContinue` over chunks then `ZSTD_compressEnd`. Vary chunk sizes\naround `ZSTD_getBlockSize()` and `ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX`. Assert byte-identical\noutput. Then decode with `ZSTD_decompressBegin` + repeated\n`ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompress` / `ZSTD_decompressContinue` driving loop, checking\n`ZSTD_nextInputType` at every step. Also cover `ZSTD_compressBegin_usingDict`,\n`ZSTD_compressBegin_advanced`, `ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict`,\n`ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDict`, `ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDDict`,\nand `ZSTD_copyCCtx` / `ZSTD_copyDCtx` (look up signatures in zstd.h).\n\n### 7. `blocklevel_compressBlock_decompressBlock_insertBlock`\n`ZSTD_getBlockSize`, `ZSTD_compressBlock`, `ZSTD_decompressBlock`,\n`ZSTD_insertBlock`. Note these operate on RAW BLOCKS (no frame). Follow the\nprotocol documented in zstd.h: `ZSTD_compressBegin` first, then `compressBlock`\nper block <= blockSize; decode with `ZSTD_decompressBegin` then `decompressBlock`.\nAssert byte-identical for every shape and for sizes 1..blockSize including\nblockSize exactly. Include the case where a block is incompressible (returns 0)\nand must be handled with `ZSTD_insertBlock`.\n\n### 8. `frame_utilities_on_valid_frames`\nFor many generated frames, `diff` these across C/Rust:\n`ZSTD_getFrameContentSize`, `ZSTD_findDecompressedSize`, `ZSTD_decompressBound`,\n`ZSTD_findFrameCompressedSize`, `ZSTD_frameHeaderSize`, `ZSTD_getFrameHeader`\n(compare the WHOLE filled struct), `ZSTD_getFrameHeader_advanced` with format 0\nand 1, `ZSTD_isFrame`, `ZSTD_isSkippableFrame`, `ZSTD_getDictID_fromFrame`,\n`ZSTD_decompressionMargin`, `ZSTD_decodingBufferSize_min`,\n`ZSTD_estimateDStreamSize_fromFrame`. Also feed each frame TRUNCATED to every\nlength from 0 to min(frameLen, 40) — the \"needs more input\" return values must\nmatch exactly.\n\n### 9. `skippable_frames`\n`ZSTD_writeSkippableFrame` (dst,dstCap,src,srcSize,magicVariant) for\nmagicVariant 0..15, `ZSTD_readSkippableFrame`, `ZSTD_isSkippableFrame`,\nand confirm `ZSTD_decompress` skips them when concatenated with real frames.\nAlso `ZSTD_writeLastEmptyBlock`.\n\n### 10. `multiframe_and_concatenation`\nConcatenate 2-5 frames (some with checksum, some skippable, some empty) and\nverify `ZSTD_decompress`, `ZSTD_decompressStream`, `ZSTD_findDecompressedSize`,\n`ZSTD_decompressBound` all agree between C and Rust.\n\n## Verify before reporting\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust\ncargo build --release 2>&1 | tail -3\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_b_streaming 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nThe file MUST COMPILE. Iterate on compile errors (check real signatures in\n`c_src/src/include/zstd.h`). Then run it and REPORT:\n- how many tests you wrote and which pass\n- for each FAILING test, the exact configuration and the C vs Rust values\n\nRemember: a failing test that reveals a genuine C/Rust divergence is a SUCCESS\nfor your task. Report it; do not hide it.","agentId":"a3f416112ac9cb696","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Created exactly one file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust/tests/phase_b_streaming.rs` (3573 lines). No other file was touched.\n\n## Result: 10 tests written, 10 pass, **0 C/Rust divergences found**\n\n```\ntest streaming_compressStream2_all_endops_and_buffer_sizes ... ok\ntest streaming_deprecated_compressStream_flush_end ......... ok\ntest streaming_decompressStream_all_buffer_sizes ........... ok\ntest streaming_with_dictionary ............................. ok\ntest streaming_stable_buffers .............................. ok\ntest blocklevel_compressBegin_continue_end ................. ok\ntest blocklevel_compressBlock_decompressBlock_insertBlock ... ok\ntest frame_utilities_on_valid_frames ....................... ok\ntest skippable_frames ...................................... ok\ntest multiframe_and_concatenation .......................... ok\ntest result: ok. 10 passed; 0 failed;  finished in 16.0s\n```\n\nInstrumented count: **7,602 differential scenarios / 6,269,442 compared API calls**, all byte- and return-code-identical.\n\n## Design\n\nEach scenario is one closure over `&Api` that records a `Trace` — the tag, return code, `input.pos` and `output.pos` after **every individual call**, plus the compressed stream and the regenerated plaintext. `diff_trace` runs it against C then Rust and reports the *first divergent call index* with surrounding context. Every test also asserts the C side round-tripped correctly, so a broken driver can't silently pass.\n\n## Harness validated with negative controls\n\nBecause everything passed, I proved the comparison actually bites by temporarily injecting `api.tag`-dependent traces:\n- differing return code → `first divergence at call #0 ... C = x{ret=1} Rust = x{ret=2}`\n- differing `cdata` → `bytes differ at index 2: C=0x03 Rust=0x04`\n- differing `out` → caught\n\nAlso confirmed coverage of the paths that are easy to miss, as hard assertions inside the tests: `assert!(nb_raw > 0)` (an incompressible block really was produced, so `ZSTD_insertBlock` is genuinely exercised), `assert!(nb_comp > 0)`, and `assert!(nb_dict_frames >= 10)` (dictID-bearing frames were really built).\n\n## Two bugs found — both in my test drivers, not the library\n\nWorth recording since they're API-contract subtleties, both confirmed against the C source rather than guessed:\n\n1. **Buffer-less decode of concatenated/skippable frames.** `ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompress() == 0` ends *one* frame, not the input (`zstd.h`: \"A frame is fully decoded when ... returns zero. Context can then be reset\"). My loop stopped after a prepended skippable frame and never decoded the real one. Fixed by re-issuing `decompressBegin*` per frame.\n2. **`ZSTD_compressBlock` emits