2` truncates `((maxSymbolValue+2)+(1<<tableLog))/2`, so for **odd `maxSymbolValue`** (e.g. 255) the macro under-reports by 2 bytes while `FSE_buildCTable_wksp`'s `spread` buffer writes 8 bytes at a time past `tableSize`. Harmless in real zstd (the workspace is a slice of the much larger `ZSTD_cwksp`), but it corrupts an exactly-sized caller allocation. Both libs overrun identically; the test allocates `SLACK_U32` extra while still passing the exact macro-computed `wkspSize`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aebf5cccec0b03c0d (use SendMessage with to: 'aebf5cccec0b03c0d', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 280076\ntool_uses: 110\nduration_ms: 2149438</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3f9022d-a72c-4fdb-a0a0-2ee15f7b56e5","uuid":"b1703b90-2636-48e7-add6-5c3a630beb4e","timestamp":"2026-08-14T22:09:48.784Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KufEFj/translated_rust\n\nYou are writing a DIFFERENTIAL TEST file for a C-to-Rust translation of zstd 1.5.7.\nThe C code is GROUND TRUTH. The Rust must match byte-for-byte.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n1. Create EXACTLY ONE new file: `tests/phase_b_dict_entropy.rs`. Do not modify any other file.\n   NEVER modify `c_src/`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`,\n   or other test files.\n2. If a test reveals C and Rust DIFFER, that is a REAL BUG in the Rust library.\n   DO NOT weaken, skip, `#[ignore]`, or loosen the assertion to make it pass.\n   DO NOT \"fix\" the test to accommodate the Rust behavior.\n   LEAVE the strict assertion and REPORT the divergence with the exact failing\n   configuration. The coordinator fixes the Rust library, not you.\n3. Never call Rust functions directly — always through the loaded `.so`.\n4. Dictionary training can be SLOW. Keep sample corpora modest (e.g. 50-200\n   samples of 256-2048 bytes) and set `nbThreads=1`. Keep total test runtime\n   under ~5 minutes. Use `steps` small (e.g. 4-8) for the \"optimize\" variants.\n\n## Existing harness (`mod common; use common::*;`)\n`tests/common/mod.rs` provides:\n- `capi()`, `rapi()` -> `&'static Api` (bundles of resolved symbols); call `(api.f)(..)` in `unsafe`.\n- `pair::<FnType>(\"Sym\") -> (c_fn, rust_fn)`; `sym::<FnType>(c_lib()|r_lib(), \"Sym\")`; `both_have(\"Sym\")`.\n- `is_error(usize)->bool`, `err_code(usize)->i64`, `err_name(lib,code)->String`,\n  `assert_bytes_eq(ctx,&[u8],&[u8])`, `assert_ret_eq(ctx,usize,usize)`,\n  `diff(ctx,|api|->T)` (T: PartialEq+Debug), `Out{ret,bytes}`, `Out::ok/err`, `diff_out`.\n- `Rng::new(seed)` `.next_u64() .next_u32() .below(n) .range(lo,hi) .byte()`.\n- `Shape::{Rle,Random,Text,Skewed,LongRange,Records}`, `ALL_SHAPES`,\n  `gen(shape,len,&mut rng)->Vec<u8>`, `gen_samples(shape,nb,min,max,&mut rng)->(Vec<u8>,Vec<usize>)`.\n- Already-declared `#[repr(C)]` structs you should USE (do not redeclare):\n  `ZDICT_params_t { compressionLevel: i32, notificationLevel: u32, dictID: u32 }`\n  `ZDICT_cover_params_t { k: u32, d: u32, steps: u32, nbThreads: u32, splitPoint: f64, shrinkDict: u32, shrinkDictMaxRegression: u32, zParams: ZDICT_params_t }`\n  `ZDICT_fastCover_params_t { k: u32, d: u32, f: u32, steps: u32, nbThreads: u32, splitPoint: f64, accel: u32, shrinkDict: u32, shrinkDictMaxRegression: u32, zParams: ZDICT_params_t }`\n  `ZDICT_legacy_params_t { selectivityLevel: u32, zParams: ZDICT_params_t }`\n  All derive `Default + Clone + Copy + Debug`.\n- `Api` has `createCCtx/freeCCtx/createDCtx/freeDCtx/compress2/compressBound/decompressDCtx/\n  setParameter/loadDictionary/refPrefix/refCDict/createCDict/freeCDict/dLoadDictionary/\n  dRefPrefix/dRefDDict/createDDict/freeDDict/getDictIDFromDict/getDictIDFromFrame/...`\n\n## What to test — CONFIGS.md rows 87-106 (dictBuilder + raw entropy + xxhash + pool)\n\nUse a FIXED SEED and multiple randomized corpora per scenario.\n\n### A. Dictionary builders — outputs must be byte-identical\nSignatures are in `c_src/src/include/zdict.h` — READ IT to get them exactly right.\n- `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer(dictBuffer, dictBufferCapacity, samplesBuffer, samplesSizes, nbSamples)`\n- `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover(..., ZDICT_cover_params_t)` — sweep k in {16,64,256,1024},\n  d in {6,8}, splitPoint 1.0, shrinkDict 0/1.\n- `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover(..., *mut ZDICT_cover_params_t)` — note it\n  WRITES BACK the chosen params: compare the mutated struct too. Use steps=4.\n- `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover(..., ZDICT_fastCover_params_t)` — sweep\n  k in {16,64,256}, d in {6,8}, f in {15,20}, accel in {1,2,10}.\n- `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover(..., *mut ZDICT_fastCover_params_t)` — steps=4,\n  compare written-back params.\n- `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_legacy(..., ZDICT_legacy_params_t)` — selectivityLevel 0..3.\n- `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary(dictBuffer, dictBufferCapacity, dictContent, dictContentSize,\n   samplesBuffer, samplesSizes, nbSamples, ZDICT_params_t)`\n- `ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer`\n- `ZDICT_getDictID(dictBuffer, dictSize)`, `ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize(dict, dictSize)`,\n  `ZDICT_isError`, `ZDICT_getErrorName`\n- The `COVER_*` exported helpers if their signatures are resolvable from\n  `c_src/src/dictBuilder/cover.h`: `COVER_sum`, `COVER_computeEpochs`,\n  `COVER_checkTotalCompressedSize`, `COVER_best_init/start/wait/finish/destroy`,\n  `COVER_dictSelectionError`, `COVER_dictSelectionIsError`, `COVER_dictSelectionFree`,\n  `COVER_selectDict`, `COVER_warnOnSmallCorpus`. Test the pure/simple ones\n  (`COVER_sum`, `COVER_computeEpochs`, `COVER_dictSelectionError/IsError`) at minimum.\n- ALSO: after training a dict with the C lib, use it to compress via BOTH libs and\n  assert byte-identical output, and assert `ZSTD_getDictID_fromDict` agrees.\n- Set `zParams.notificationLevel = 0` everywhere to keep stderr quiet, and use\n  `nbThreads = 1`.\n\n### B. Raw FSE entry points (declared in `c_src/src/common/fse.h`)\n`diff` these across C/Rust over randomized histograms/inputs:\n- `FSE_compressBound`, `FSE_NCountWriteBound`, `FSE_optimalTableLog`,\n  `FSE_optimalTableLog_internal`, `FSE_normalizeCount`, `FSE_writeNCount`,\n  `FSE_readNCount`, `FSE_readNCount_bmi2`, `FSE_buildCTable_wksp`,\n  `FSE_buildCTable_rle`, `FSE_compress_usingCTable`, `FSE_buildDTable_wksp`,\n  `FSE_decompress_wksp`, `FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2`, `FSE_versionNumber`,\n  `FSE_isError`, `FSE_getErrorName`.\nBuild histograms with `HIST_count` first. Compare the FULL contents of any\noutput buffer/table (cast to `&[u8]` of the right byte length), not just returns.\nRound-trip: normalizeCount -> writeNCount -> readNCount must give back the same\ncounts in both libs.\n\n### C. Raw HUF entry points (`c_src/src/common/huf.h`)\n- `HUF_compressBound`, `HUF_optimalTableLog`, `HUF_minTableLog`, `HUF_cardinality`,\n  `HUF_buildCTable_wksp`, `HUF_writeCTable_wksp`, `HUF_readCTable`,\n  `HUF_readCTableHeader`, `HUF_validateCTable`, `HUF_getNbBitsFromCTable`,\n  `HUF_estimateCompressedSize`, `HUF_compress1X_usingCTable`,\n  `HUF_compress4X_usingCTable`, `HUF_compress1X_repeat`, `HUF_compress4X_repeat`,\n  `HUF_decompress1X_usingDTable`, `HUF_decompress4X_usingDTable`,\n  `HUF_readDTableX1_wksp`, `HUF_readDTableX2_wksp`, `HUF_decompress1X1_DCtx_wksp`,\n  `HUF_decompress1X2_DCtx_wksp`, `HUF_decompress1X_DCtx_wksp`,\n  `HUF_decompress4X_hufOnly_wksp`, `HUF_selectDecoder`, `HUF_readStats`,\n  `HUF_readStats_wksp`, `HUF_isError`, `HUF_getErrorName`.\nCompare returns AND all output bytes AND written table contents. Round-trip\ncompress->decompress through both libs.\n\n### D. HIST entry points (`c_src/src/compress/hist.h`)\n`HIST_count`, `HIST_countFast`, `HIST_count_simple`, `HIST_count_wksp`,\n`HIST_countFast_wksp`, `HIST_add`, `HIST_isError`. Compare the full count array\n(maxSymbolValue+1 u32s) and the returned max-count, over all `Shape`s and many\nsizes including 0 and 1.\n\n### E. xxhash (namespaced `ZSTD_XXH*`)\n`ZSTD_XXH32`, `ZSTD_XXH64` one-shot over